1
00:00:01,735 --> 00:00:03,772
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,805 --> 00:00:06,808
♪ WAY DOWN IN DEEP 13 ♪

3
00:00:06,842 --> 00:00:09,977
♪ DR. FORRESTER
AND TV'S FRANK ♪

4
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:13,180
♪ WERE HATCHING
AN EVIL SCHEME ♪

5
00:00:13,213 --> 00:00:16,250
♪ THEY HIRED A TEMP
BY THE NAME OF MIKE ♪

6
00:00:16,283 --> 00:00:19,387
♪ JUST A REGULAR JOE
THEY DIDN'T LIKE ♪

7
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:22,357
♪ THEIR EXPERIMENT
NEEDED A GOOD TEST CASE ♪

8
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,092
♪ SO THEY CONKED HIM
ON THE NOGGIN ♪

9
00:00:24,125 --> 00:00:26,027
♪ AND THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:28,697
GET ME DOWN!

11
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:31,833
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

12
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:35,002
♪ THE WORST WE CAN
FIND-- LA LA LA ♪

13
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,905
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:37,938 --> 00:00:41,275
♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR
HIS MIND-- LA LA LA ♪

15
00:00:41,308 --> 00:00:44,112
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND,
MIKE CAN'T CONTROL ♪

16
00:00:44,145 --> 00:00:47,448
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES BEGIN
OR END-- LA LA LA ♪

17
00:00:47,482 --> 00:00:50,518
♪ HE'LL TRY TO KEEP
HIS SANITY ♪

18
00:00:50,552 --> 00:00:53,855
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

19
00:00:55,623 --> 00:00:57,025
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL ♪

20
00:00:57,058 --> 00:00:58,527
CAMBOT!

21
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,793
GYPSY!

22
00:00:59,827 --> 00:01:01,695
TOM SERVO!

23
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:02,963
CROW!

24
00:01:02,997 --> 00:01:04,432
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW ♪

25
00:01:04,465 --> 00:01:06,267
♪ HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

26
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,370
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE
FACTS-- LA LA LA ♪

27
00:01:09,403 --> 00:01:12,407
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

28
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:15,343
♪ I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

29
00:01:15,377 --> 00:01:18,412
♪ FOR MYSTERY
SCIENCE THEATER ♪

30
00:01:18,445 --> 00:01:21,582
♪ 3000 ♪

31
00:01:35,597 --> 00:01:38,098
[CROW GASPS]

32
00:01:40,835 --> 00:01:42,403
HI, EVERYONE, I'M MIKE.

33
00:01:42,437 --> 00:01:43,638
WELCOME TO THE SAT--

34
00:01:43,672 --> 00:01:46,240
AAH! CROW,
WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

35
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:47,875
YOU LIKE THE LOOK?

36
00:01:47,908 --> 00:01:49,677
I GOT CONTACT LENSES.

37
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:50,878
BUT YOUR EYES WERE FINE.

38
00:01:50,912 --> 00:01:52,647
REALLY WORKING OUT
FOR ME, TOO.

39
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,982
YEAH, I SEE THAT.

40
00:01:54,015 --> 00:01:55,550
YEP, EVERY 15 MINUTES,

41
00:01:55,583 --> 00:01:57,285
I TAKE THEM OUT,
RINSE THEM,

42
00:01:57,318 --> 00:01:59,287
SOAK THEM,
THEN POP THEM BACK IN

43
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:01,122
FOR MORE EASY VIEWING.

44
00:02:01,155 --> 00:02:03,323
SO MUCH EASIER
THAN GLASSES.

45
00:02:03,357 --> 00:02:05,727
AND-- AND YOU'RE NOT
GONNA BLINK ANYMORE.

46
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:07,195
THESE ARE SOFT CONTACTS.

47
00:02:07,228 --> 00:02:09,197
YOU DON'T HAVE TO BLINK.

48
00:02:09,230 --> 00:02:11,532
WE'LL BE BACK IN A SEC.

49
00:02:11,565 --> 00:02:13,033
THEY LOOK PAINFUL.

50
00:02:13,067 --> 00:02:14,235
NO, UGH.

51
00:02:21,375 --> 00:02:22,810
IT'S OKAY, AH,
THERE WE GO.

52
00:02:22,843 --> 00:02:25,012
ALL RIGHT, SHH,
NO, BE STILL.

53
00:02:25,045 --> 00:02:26,780
OH, SEE,
THAT'S YOUR PROBLEM.

54
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:29,017
OKAY, OH, AHH.

55
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:30,352
OH, THAT'S WHERE
THAT ONE WENT.

56
00:02:30,385 --> 00:02:31,785
THERE, CAN YOU SEE
A LITTLE BETTER NOW?

57
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:33,020
OH, I DON'T
THINK SO, MIKE.

58
00:02:33,053 --> 00:02:34,455
THESE CONTACTS
MUST BE FAULTY,

59
00:02:34,488 --> 00:02:36,723
BECAUSE SERVO LOOKS LIKE
HE HAS SNEAKERS ON.

60
00:02:36,757 --> 00:02:39,260
WELL, THAT'S OBVIOUSLY WRONG,
BECAUSE HE-- AAH!

61
00:02:39,293 --> 00:02:40,495
SERVO, WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

62
00:02:40,528 --> 00:02:41,662
GUESS WHAT, MIKE?
JUST SIGNED MYSELF

63
00:02:41,695 --> 00:02:43,497
A MILLION DOLLAR
CONTRACT TO ENDORSE

64
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:45,098
THESE DESIGNER SNEAKERS.

65
00:02:45,132 --> 00:02:46,500
BUT HOW CAN THAT BE?
YOU DON'T--

66
00:02:46,533 --> 00:02:47,768
HAVE ANY FEET?

67
00:02:47,802 --> 00:02:49,170
I KNOW,
BUT THAT DOESN'T MATTER.

68
00:02:49,203 --> 00:02:51,572
I DON'T NEED FEET.
I'M ALL CHARISMA.

69
00:02:51,605 --> 00:02:53,440
NOW THAT TV'S FRANK
IS MY AGENT,

70
00:02:53,473 --> 00:02:54,875
THE OPPORTUNITIES
ARE LIMITLESS.

71
00:02:54,908 --> 00:02:56,443
TV'S FRANK IS AN AGENT?

72
00:02:56,477 --> 00:02:58,713
WELL, SURE,
HE'S HANDLING ACTORS,

73
00:02:58,747 --> 00:03:00,648
DIRECTORS, SCREENWRITERS--

74
00:03:00,682 --> 00:03:02,617
SCREENWRITERS?! AAH!

75
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,422
HELLO, TV'S FRANK.

76
00:03:07,455 --> 00:03:08,555
COME IN, MY GOOD BUDDY.

77
00:03:08,588 --> 00:03:10,658
COME IN, WONDERFUL
FRANK OF MINE.

78
00:03:10,692 --> 00:03:12,927
MM-HMM, YEAH,
OKAY, BINKY.

79
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:15,597
THANKS A LOT, HONEY.
I'LL GET BACK TO YOU. THANKS.

80
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:16,998
TALK TO ME.

81
00:03:17,032 --> 00:03:19,433
OH, HI, JEFFREY.
HI, STEVEN.

82
00:03:19,467 --> 00:03:21,002
HI, DAVID.
LOOK, I'VE BEEN

83
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:22,903
THINKING THIS OVER,
AND IF I'M GONNA

84
00:03:22,937 --> 00:03:24,905
HELP YOU WITH
THIS NEW PROJECT,

85
00:03:24,938 --> 00:03:27,108
FRANKLY, I'M GONNA HAVE
TO SEE SOME RESUMES.

86
00:03:27,142 --> 00:03:29,410
I'M SORRY, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU'VE DONE.

87
00:03:29,443 --> 00:03:32,013
I-- GOODBYE!

88
00:03:32,047 --> 00:03:35,450
YEAH? CROW T-BABY,
TALK TO ME.

89
00:03:35,483 --> 00:03:38,953
FRANK, YOU'VE READ MY SPEC
SCREENPLAYS, RIGHT?

90
00:03:38,987 --> 00:03:40,688
EARTH VS. SOUP,
AND, OF COURSE,

91
00:03:40,722 --> 00:03:43,792
MY PETER GRAVES AT THE
UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA SCRIPT.

92
00:03:43,825 --> 00:03:45,025
NOW THAT YOU'RE
A BIG-TIME AGENT,

93
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,193
HOW ABOUT REPRESENTING ME?

94
00:03:46,227 --> 00:03:48,095
CROW, I'VE READ
EARTH VS. SOUP,

95
00:03:48,128 --> 00:03:50,230
AND, FRANKLY,
IT'S A BIG SO-WHAT.

96
00:03:50,263 --> 00:03:51,632
AS FOR THAT OTHER THING,

97
00:03:51,665 --> 00:03:53,200
WELL, SEVERAL STUDIOS

98
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,268
ALL OVER TOWN
ARE DEVELOPING THEIR OWN

99
00:03:55,302 --> 00:03:57,838
PETER GRAVES AT THE
UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA
PROJECTS.

100
00:03:57,872 --> 00:03:59,607
SO, I'M AFRAID
I DON'T THINK I CAN--

101
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,177
[CROW SOBS]

102
00:04:03,678 --> 00:04:04,945
FRANK, I THINK
IT'S AWFUL HOW

103
00:04:04,978 --> 00:04:06,747
YOU'VE BECOME
THIS PHONY, FLASHY

104
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:08,282
HOLLYWOOD WHEELER-DEALER.

105
00:04:08,315 --> 00:04:09,883
PERSONALLY, I'LL HAVE
NO PART OF IT.

106
00:04:09,917 --> 00:04:11,918
MIKE, I'VE BEEN
WANTING TO TALK TO YOU.

107
00:04:11,952 --> 00:04:13,120
I'VE GOT YOU BOOKED TO TOUR

108
00:04:13,153 --> 00:04:15,255
ON ANYTHING GOES
AT TEN GRAND A POP.

109
00:04:15,288 --> 00:04:18,158
♪ IN OLDEN DAYS
A GLIMPSE OF STOCKING ♪

110
00:04:18,192 --> 00:04:20,060
♪ WAS THOUGHT OF AS
SOMETHING SHOCKING ♪

111
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:22,530
♪ NOW HEAVEN KNOWS ♪

112
00:04:22,563 --> 00:04:23,898
IT'S A DONE DEAL,
A NO-BRAINER.

113
00:04:23,932 --> 00:04:26,100
LOOK, AT THE END OF THE DAY,
WE'RE ALL GOING TO--

114
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:27,402
- FRANK!
- WHAT?

115
00:04:27,435 --> 00:04:29,070
FRANK, WHAT TH--

116
00:04:29,103 --> 00:04:30,472
WHAT'RE YOU DOING?

117
00:04:30,505 --> 00:04:32,140
CLAY, GET ME SOME
PELLEGRINO, WILL YOU?

118
00:04:32,173 --> 00:04:34,208
I'VE GOT COLEMAN FRANCIS
ON THE LINE.

119
00:04:34,242 --> 00:04:35,977
[DOORBELL RINGS]

120
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:37,712
OH, THAT'S MY 4:00!

121
00:04:37,745 --> 00:04:39,080
OH, BOY,

122
00:04:39,113 --> 00:04:42,050
MY HOTTEST NEW CLIENT
HAS ARRIVED!

123
00:04:42,083 --> 00:04:45,018
TORGY, BABY! HOW YOU DOING?

124
00:04:45,052 --> 00:04:48,155
GREAT TO BE
WORKING WITH YOU.

125
00:04:48,188 --> 00:04:49,690
THE MASTER WILL BE PLEASED

126
00:04:49,723 --> 00:04:51,458
IF I GET PAY-AND-PLAY

127
00:04:51,492 --> 00:04:54,062
AND BACK-END PARTICIPATION.

128
00:04:54,095 --> 00:04:56,830
ALL RIGHT, UH, CLAY,
MY PELLEGRINO?

129
00:04:56,863 --> 00:04:58,700
TORGY, IT'S GREAT
TO BE WORKING WITH YOU.

130
00:04:58,733 --> 00:05:00,568
YOU KNOW,
THIS IS ESSENTIALLY

131
00:05:00,602 --> 00:05:02,603
A BUSINESS ABOUT
RELATIONSHIPS.

132
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:09,743
AS OF NOW, I'M CLOSING
FRANK'S LITTLE OFFICE.

133
00:05:09,777 --> 00:05:12,380
I'M CANCELING
YOUR CONTRACTS.

134
00:05:12,413 --> 00:05:14,848
BUT I'M TAKING ON
DANGER!! DEATH RAY

135
00:05:14,882 --> 00:05:16,117
AS A CLIENT.

136
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:17,818
IN FACT, I'M BOOKING IT

137
00:05:17,852 --> 00:05:20,588
AS THIS WEEK'S EXPERIMENT.

138
00:05:20,622 --> 00:05:21,855
YES, GENTLEMEN.

139
00:05:21,888 --> 00:05:23,457
PREPARE TO TAKE A MEETING

140
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:26,693
WITH EXTREME EMOTIONAL PAIN.

141
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:31,832
DO YOU HAVE
MIKE OVITZ'S NUMBER?

142
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:35,035
♪ YOU'RE THE TOP ♪

143
00:05:35,068 --> 00:05:36,570
♪ YOU'RE THE TOWER OF PISA ♪

144
00:05:36,603 --> 00:05:38,505
- ♪ YOU'RE THE TOP ♪
- SNAP OUT OF IT, THERE.

145
00:05:38,538 --> 00:05:41,108
- ♪ YOU'RE THE MONA LISA ♪
- WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

146
00:05:53,822 --> 00:05:55,523
CRAZY NUT.

147
00:05:55,557 --> 00:05:58,793
LOOK AT YOU.
YOU LOOK RIDICULOUS.

148
00:05:58,827 --> 00:06:01,962
[JAZZ MUSIC]

149
00:06:01,995 --> 00:06:05,032
IN THE BAH-BADA-BA-DABA
STORY.

150
00:06:05,065 --> 00:06:06,667
OH, I'M GLAD
THEY SAID DANGER.

151
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,103
I MIGHT'VE THOUGHT IT WAS
JUST A NORMAL DEATH RAY.

152
00:06:09,137 --> 00:06:11,172
THERE IS A DANGEROUS
DEATH RAY SITUATION

153
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:12,340
ON OUTBOUND 94.

154
00:06:12,373 --> 00:06:15,543
YOU MIGHT WANNA TAKE
AN ALTERNATE ROUTE.

155
00:06:15,577 --> 00:06:18,478
WHICH ONE OF THESE GUYS IS
MARCELLO MASTROIANNI?

156
00:06:20,515 --> 00:06:22,082
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU
SPENT THE WHOLE PARTY

157
00:06:22,115 --> 00:06:24,818
TALKING TO THAT GUY.

158
00:06:24,852 --> 00:06:28,355
DRIVER, WILL YOU TELL HIM
I'M NOT TALKING TO HIM?

159
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:30,425
AH, THE HANDSOME ONE
OF THE GROUP.

160
00:06:32,327 --> 00:06:34,462
ITALY'S TOR JOHNSON.

161
00:06:38,665 --> 00:06:40,535
- DING!
- [ALL HUM TO THEME]

162
00:06:42,837 --> 00:06:46,040
I THINK HAL DAVID
WROTE THE LYRICS.

163
00:06:46,073 --> 00:06:48,542
♪ LET'S GO SWINGIN'
IN THE NIGHT ♪

164
00:06:52,045 --> 00:06:53,647
WHAT DO THEY MEAN BY
BAH-BADA-BA-DABA?

165
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,517
IS IT PROTEST?

166
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:58,318
IT WAS ORIGINALLY TITLED
"LA LALA LA LALA."

167
00:06:58,352 --> 00:07:00,855
BIG CREATIVE DISPUTE.

168
00:07:00,888 --> 00:07:02,557
HERE IT COMES AGAIN.

169
00:07:02,590 --> 00:07:04,992
- BING!
- BAH-BADA-BA-DABA.

170
00:07:07,895 --> 00:07:09,997
IF MICHAEL CAINE
AND ANDRE THE GIANT

171
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:12,733
HAD A CHILD.

172
00:07:12,767 --> 00:07:15,235
OH, LOOK AT THAT.

173
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,605
MAKE-A-FACE!
DESIGN YOUR OWN FACE.

174
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:23,043
I SHOULD LIKE TO BE
IN A BARBERSHOP QUARTET.

175
00:07:23,077 --> 00:07:24,378
BING.

176
00:07:24,412 --> 00:07:26,513
THESE ARE, LIKE,
EUROPEAN REGULAR GUYS.

177
00:07:26,547 --> 00:07:28,382
BUT EUROPEAN REGULAR GUYS
ARE STILL

178
00:07:28,415 --> 00:07:30,518
A LOT COOLER THAN
AMERICAN REGULAR GUYS.

179
00:07:30,552 --> 00:07:32,920
THESE MEN ARE
READY FOR ACTION.

180
00:07:32,953 --> 00:07:36,523
WOMEN ADORE THEM,
MEN RESPECT THEM.

181
00:07:36,557 --> 00:07:39,093
WHAT? WHAT?
THEY'RE LOOKING AT ME.

182
00:07:39,127 --> 00:07:41,062
I'M NOT LOOKING.

183
00:07:44,332 --> 00:07:46,733
GET THIS OFF
YOUR HEAD PLEASE.

184
00:07:46,767 --> 00:07:50,070
- BOTHERING YOU?
- YES.

185
00:07:50,103 --> 00:07:52,707
THEY'RE AT THE END OF
THE BAH-BADA-BA-DABA TOUR.

186
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:55,543
THAT WAS "BAH-BADA-BA-DABA"
BY THE DOODLETOWN PIPERS.

187
00:07:56,877 --> 00:07:59,313
BAH-BADA-BA-DABA?

188
00:07:59,347 --> 00:08:02,950
YOU GIVIN' ME A TICKET?

189
00:08:02,983 --> 00:08:04,185
OKAY, EVERYTHING'S IN ORDER.

190
00:08:04,218 --> 00:08:05,352
LET THEM THROUGH.

191
00:08:05,385 --> 00:08:06,820
WHAT COUNTRY
IS THIS TAKING PLACE IN?

192
00:08:06,853 --> 00:08:08,522
EUROPE.

193
00:08:11,925 --> 00:08:15,228
I LIKE TO WATCH PEOPLE PARK.

194
00:08:15,262 --> 00:08:17,163
♪ HI-HO, HI-HO ♪

195
00:08:17,197 --> 00:08:20,635
♪ IT'S OFF TO WORK WE GO ♪

196
00:08:20,668 --> 00:08:22,970
MINI-DISH HASN'T MADE
HIS LIFE ANY BETTER.

197
00:08:28,075 --> 00:08:30,010
OKAY?!

198
00:08:31,245 --> 00:08:33,915
BIFF, MOFF, HI.

199
00:08:33,948 --> 00:08:35,583
ALL THIS EQUIPMENT JUST
TO CATCH RERUNS

200
00:08:35,617 --> 00:08:38,618
OF MADAM'S PLACE.

201
00:08:38,652 --> 00:08:40,120
LOOKS LIKE SOMETHING
MY DAD WOULD BUY

202
00:08:40,153 --> 00:08:42,723
AT A GARAGE SALE.

203
00:08:42,757 --> 00:08:44,692
MERV'S GUESTS
ARE ZSA ZSA GABOR,

204
00:08:44,725 --> 00:08:47,227
THE DEATH RAY,
AND TONY FIELDS.

205
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:49,963
WELP, THE REASON I GAVE
YOUR PAPER A "D" IS BECAUSE--

206
00:08:52,032 --> 00:08:53,433
PROFESSOR CARMICHAEL, SIR?

207
00:08:53,467 --> 00:08:55,637
THE COMMISSIONERS
ARE ALL PRESENT.

208
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:57,505
THE NATO COMMISSION'S
ALL PRESENT.

209
00:08:57,538 --> 00:08:58,940
LET'S BEGIN, THEN.

210
00:08:58,973 --> 00:09:00,775
HAVE DOCTOR CARVER
BRING THAT IN, PLEASE.

211
00:09:00,808 --> 00:09:02,643
BAH-BADA-BA-DABA.

212
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:09,217
THIS IS YOUR LIFE,
JEAN PAUL BELMONDO!

213
00:09:09,250 --> 00:09:11,118
AH, THE WORLDPERKS CLUB.

214
00:09:11,152 --> 00:09:12,453
GOOD EVENING, GENTLEMEN.

215
00:09:12,487 --> 00:09:14,122
IT'S REALLY QUITE
EUROPEAN IN HERE.

216
00:09:14,155 --> 00:09:17,090
PROFESSOR CARMICHAEL
IS WAITING FOR YOU.

217
00:09:17,123 --> 00:09:20,060
WE DIDN'T GET
OUR DRINKS YET.

218
00:09:20,093 --> 00:09:21,328
THOSE OF YOU
WITH SMALL CHILDREN

219
00:09:21,362 --> 00:09:23,830
WILL PLEASE BOARD
PROFESSOR CARMICHAEL FIRST.

220
00:09:26,867 --> 00:09:29,603
[ALL MURMUR]

221
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:38,745
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
YOUR PASTY WHITE EUROPEANS.

222
00:09:40,982 --> 00:09:44,485
BUCKAROO BANZAI GOES
TO THE NURSING HOME.

223
00:09:44,518 --> 00:09:46,353
THEY REALLY HAVE
CAPTURED THE GRANDEUR

224
00:09:46,387 --> 00:09:48,655
OF WHITE GUYS
WALKING IN HERDS.

225
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,625
PLEASE.

226
00:09:51,658 --> 00:09:54,062
AFTER YOU, SWIFTY.

227
00:09:54,095 --> 00:09:56,397
THIS SCENE COULD REALLY
USE A BAH-BADA-BA-DADA.

228
00:09:58,798 --> 00:10:02,570
- BARRY DILLER!
- IT IS.

229
00:10:02,603 --> 00:10:05,272
[RASPBERRY] OH NO,
NOT ONE OF MY ATTACKS.

230
00:10:05,305 --> 00:10:09,010
NOT HERE IN THE ELEVATOR.

231
00:10:09,043 --> 00:10:10,477
AREN'T YOU GLAD
YOU USED DIAL?

232
00:10:10,510 --> 00:10:13,613
DON'T YOU WISH
EUROPEANS DID?

233
00:10:13,647 --> 00:10:14,882
[IMITATING FLATULENCE]

234
00:10:14,915 --> 00:10:17,552
UH, PERHAPS SOMEONE SHOULD
PRESS A FLOOR BUTTON.

235
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:22,523
BIFF, MOFF, LET ME FLIP
ONE OF THESE SWITCHES HERE.

236
00:10:24,023 --> 00:10:26,493
YOU'RE WATCHING
BRIAN TELEVISION.

237
00:10:26,527 --> 00:10:30,297
ALL BRIAN, ALL THE TIME.

238
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:31,565
IN AN UNDERGROUND BUNKER,

239
00:10:31,598 --> 00:10:35,068
THE MAJOR LEAGUE OWNERS
PLOT STRATEGY.

240
00:10:35,102 --> 00:10:37,738
WHY CAN'T I GET
THE RED SHOE DIARIES?

241
00:10:41,342 --> 00:10:43,143
SIT DOWN, PLEASE,
GENTLEMEN, GOOD EVENING.

242
00:10:43,177 --> 00:10:44,412
THANK YOU FOR COMING, YES,

243
00:10:44,445 --> 00:10:46,613
ALL OF YOU
CAN BE HAND MODELS.

244
00:10:49,083 --> 00:10:52,687
I THINK THEY NEED TO LOOSEN UP
THEIR FAMILY REUNION.

245
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:54,722
ALL RIGHT, NOW,
WHO HERE IS BALD?

246
00:10:54,755 --> 00:10:57,257
SHOW OF HANDS, PLEASE?

247
00:10:57,290 --> 00:10:58,992
GENTLEMEN, I SHOULD
LIKE TO REMIND YOU,

248
00:10:59,025 --> 00:11:00,660
FIRST OF ALL,
THAT THE DEMONSTRATION

249
00:11:00,693 --> 00:11:02,863
YOU'RE ABOUT TO WITNESS
IS TOP SECRET.

250
00:11:02,897 --> 00:11:05,565
THE REASON FOR THIS
WILL SOON BE OBVIOUS.

251
00:11:05,598 --> 00:11:07,668
- IT'S IN MY PANTS.
- I DON'T NEED TO WARN YOU

252
00:11:07,702 --> 00:11:09,870
THAT YOU'RE RESPONSIBLE
TO YOUR RESPECTIVE GOVERNMENTS

253
00:11:09,903 --> 00:11:11,205
FOR SECURITY IN THIS MATTER.

254
00:11:11,238 --> 00:11:12,973
ISN'T THIS
THE REAL ESTATE SEMINAR?

255
00:11:13,007 --> 00:11:14,275
I'VE DEDICATED
THE WHOLE OF MY LIFE

256
00:11:14,308 --> 00:11:16,043
TO THE STUDY
OF RADIATION AND--

257
00:11:16,077 --> 00:11:18,645
- CROCHETING.
- ITS USE FOR MEDICINE.

258
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:20,247
BUT I FIND THAT
THE MORAL CONCEPTS

259
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,850
THAT HAVE GOVERNED ALL
MY WORK IN THE PAST

260
00:11:22,883 --> 00:11:24,452
NO LONGER APPLY TODAY.

261
00:11:24,485 --> 00:11:25,618
YOU'RE NOT FUNNY!

262
00:11:25,652 --> 00:11:27,788
UNFORTUNATELY,
MY WORK ON RADIATION

263
00:11:27,822 --> 00:11:31,058
IS AS DANGEROUS AS THE DISCOVERY
OF ATOMIC ENERGY WAS.

264
00:11:31,092 --> 00:11:32,460
ISN'T THAT RADIATION TOO?

265
00:11:32,493 --> 00:11:34,595
IT MAY EVEN CONTRIBUTE
TO THE WELL-BEING OF MAN,

266
00:11:34,628 --> 00:11:36,230
OR BRING ABOUT
HIS DESTRUCTION.

267
00:11:36,263 --> 00:11:37,965
COME ON,
DEATH RAY SOMETHING!

268
00:11:37,998 --> 00:11:40,400
AS A SCIENTIST,
NATURALLY I COULDN'T IGNORE

269
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:42,168
MY PERSONAL
RESPONSIBILITY...

270
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:44,405
- RIBBIT, RIBBIT.
- ...IN THIS TERRIBLE CHOICE.

271
00:11:44,438 --> 00:11:47,307
AND SO I FELT THAT,
FROM AN ETHICAL POINT OF VIEW,

272
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:49,577
IT WAS MY DUTY
TO USE THIS KNOWLEDGE

273
00:11:49,610 --> 00:11:52,012
NOT ONLY FOR
THE TREATMENT OF DISEASE,

274
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:54,115
BUT TO DEVELOP
A POWERFUL WEAPON

275
00:11:54,148 --> 00:11:56,550
THAT MIGHT SERVE
AS A DETERRENT

276
00:11:56,583 --> 00:11:59,453
TO THE PRESERVATION
OF WORLD PEACE.

277
00:11:59,487 --> 00:12:01,488
RIBBIT.

278
00:12:01,522 --> 00:12:03,723
- IS ANYONE LISTENING?
- I SUCCEEDED.

279
00:12:03,757 --> 00:12:06,927
WHICH IS THE REASON WHY YOU'VE
BEEN INVITED HERE TONIGHT.

280
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,195
PLEASE PAY CAREFUL ATTENTION

281
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:10,230
TO EVERYTHING
YOU'RE GOING TO SEE.

282
00:12:10,263 --> 00:12:12,098
SURE IT'S PHALLIC,
WHY WOULDN'T IT BE?

283
00:12:14,235 --> 00:12:16,737
THE POWER OF DISINTEGRATION
OF THIS RAY

284
00:12:16,770 --> 00:12:18,438
IS A LOT GREATER
THAN A LASER BEAM.

285
00:12:18,472 --> 00:12:21,475
SO I HAVEN'T JUST
INVENTED THAT AGAIN.

286
00:12:21,508 --> 00:12:23,410
GENTLEMEN, IT IS MY
EARNEST WISH

287
00:12:23,443 --> 00:12:24,612
THAT THIS INSTRUMENT

288
00:12:24,645 --> 00:12:27,113
WHICH WE HAVE
FINALLY DEVELOPED HERE

289
00:12:27,147 --> 00:12:29,115
MAY NEVER HAVE TO BE
USED FOR ANYTHING

290
00:12:29,148 --> 00:12:31,118
BUT A PURELY
PEACEFUL PURPOSE.

291
00:12:31,152 --> 00:12:32,553
- [SERVO CHUCKLES]
- THE CHOICE IS NOT MINE.

292
00:12:32,587 --> 00:12:35,055
- IT'S MY WIFE'S.
- OPEN THE DOORS.

293
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:38,358
SO IT'S A PEACE-LOVING
DEATH RAY.

294
00:12:38,392 --> 00:12:41,428
THAT USED TO BE MY JOB.

295
00:12:41,462 --> 00:12:43,963
THIS THE DEATH FUSE BOX.

296
00:12:47,902 --> 00:12:51,105
OH, AND OUR DOORS "MOO"
WHEN YOU OPEN THEM.

297
00:12:51,138 --> 00:12:52,305
I RESTATE AGAIN,

298
00:12:52,338 --> 00:12:54,073
IT'S FOR PEACEFUL PURPOSES.

299
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:55,943
THAT IS A BLOCK OF
THE SPECIAL STEEL ALLOY

300
00:12:55,977 --> 00:12:57,210
USED IN SPACECRAFT,

301
00:12:57,243 --> 00:12:58,845
AND IS, AS A CONSEQUENCE,

302
00:12:58,878 --> 00:13:01,648
EXCEPTIONALLY RESISTANT
TO VERY HIGH PRESSURE STRESS

303
00:13:01,682 --> 00:13:03,250
AND EXTRA-ATMOSPHERIC
TEMPERATURES.

304
00:13:03,283 --> 00:13:04,518
PENCIL DROP AT 9:15.

305
00:13:04,552 --> 00:13:05,887
I OUGHT TO EXPLAIN TO YOU

306
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:08,122
THAT THE RAY I'M GOING
TO USE IN THIS EXPERIMENT

307
00:13:08,155 --> 00:13:09,823
IS ONLY ONE HUNDREDTH
OF THE MAXIMUM POWER

308
00:13:09,857 --> 00:13:11,258
THAT CAN BE OBTAINED.

309
00:13:11,292 --> 00:13:13,193
- TURN IT ON!
- BUT TO CREATE
A MORE POTENT RAY,

310
00:13:13,227 --> 00:13:15,295
IT'S NOT NECESSARY TO BUILD
A BIGGER APPARATUS.

311
00:13:15,328 --> 00:13:16,997
- COME ON!
- FOR GREATER INTENSITY,

312
00:13:17,030 --> 00:13:18,632
IT'S ENOUGH
TO TURN THIS CONTROL.

313
00:13:18,665 --> 00:13:22,637
CAN THE...
AND KILL SOMETHING!

314
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:24,638
SO THIS IS MARTINIZING.

315
00:13:28,208 --> 00:13:29,377
AAH, AAH, AGAIN,

316
00:13:29,410 --> 00:13:31,478
PEACEFUL PURPOSES.

317
00:13:31,512 --> 00:13:34,882
I'VE SEEN BETTER
DEATH RAYS.

318
00:13:34,915 --> 00:13:36,350
NOW, YOU MIGHT
EXPECT TO PAY

319
00:13:36,383 --> 00:13:38,818
UP TO $3 MILLION FOR
A DEATH RAY LIKE THIS.

320
00:13:38,852 --> 00:13:40,553
BUT WAIT!

321
00:13:40,587 --> 00:13:44,190
STILL THOUGHT
THERE'D BE DONUTS.

322
00:13:44,223 --> 00:13:46,560
RIBBIT.

323
00:13:46,593 --> 00:13:48,662
HEY, MY CAR'S PARKED
BEHIND THAT WALL!

324
00:13:50,730 --> 00:13:52,733
DANGER! BIFOCALS.

325
00:13:54,368 --> 00:13:56,103
SO, IF YOU EVER NEED
TO BURN HOLES IN STUFF,

326
00:13:56,137 --> 00:13:59,072
THIS IS YOUR BABY.

327
00:13:59,105 --> 00:14:00,373
I DON'T LIKE THAT,
BUT I'LL TAKE

328
00:14:00,407 --> 00:14:02,910
A DOZEN OF THOSE
LITTLE SWITCHES.

329
00:14:02,943 --> 00:14:06,080
[CROWD MURMURS]

330
00:14:06,113 --> 00:14:08,382
ON BEHALF OF THE UGLY
EUROPEAN SOCIETY,

331
00:14:08,415 --> 00:14:10,417
WE APPLAUD YOU.

332
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:13,587
HE'S SEXY WITHOUT
HIS GLASSES.

333
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:17,257
OH NO, IT'S FDS!

334
00:14:17,290 --> 00:14:19,192
WELL, THIS FROSTS
MY STRAWBERRIES.

335
00:14:19,225 --> 00:14:21,495
- [GUNSHOT]
- OH, MY GALLSTONE!

336
00:14:23,997 --> 00:14:26,033
OH, BUTTERFINGERS,
I'M SORRY.

337
00:14:28,435 --> 00:14:31,138
QUICK, IT'S
THE EMERGENCY ALARM!

338
00:14:31,172 --> 00:14:32,272
THEY WENT TO THE LABORATORY.

339
00:14:32,305 --> 00:14:34,508
REALLY QUEER
EMERGENCY ALARM.

340
00:14:43,783 --> 00:14:45,385
OH, THIS IS OUR
FIRST EMERGENCY.

341
00:14:45,418 --> 00:14:48,022
WE'RE NOT VERY GOOD.

342
00:14:48,055 --> 00:14:50,723
PECKINPAH'S
WILD PARKING ATTENDANTS.

343
00:14:52,827 --> 00:14:54,060
WOULD YOU PLEASE
TURN OFF THE ALARM?

344
00:14:54,093 --> 00:14:56,363
IT'S JUST
MAKING US ALL TENSE.

345
00:14:56,397 --> 00:14:57,632
IT'S THE NUMBERS
FOR THE BABYSITTER,

346
00:14:57,665 --> 00:15:00,700
THE POLICE, AND THE MARONIS
NEXT DOOR.

347
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,837
POLICE HEADQUARTERS?

348
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:04,938
- EMERGENCY.
- WE CAN'T GET THE ALARM OFF.

349
00:15:04,972 --> 00:15:06,040
THE LABORATORY
IS UNDER ATTACK.

350
00:15:13,647 --> 00:15:15,715
AW, HE HAD A LITTLE
TOO MUCH DEATH RAY.

351
00:15:19,185 --> 00:15:21,122
OH, THE GROOVIE GHOULIES
ARE AFTER THEM.

352
00:15:28,562 --> 00:15:30,430
IS THAT TOO MANY BULLETS
BACK THERE?

353
00:15:30,463 --> 00:15:33,700
IS THAT OKAY?

354
00:15:33,733 --> 00:15:36,470
ENJOY MY TEETH.

355
00:15:36,503 --> 00:15:37,772
UH, I'M AFRAID YOU WON'T

356
00:15:37,805 --> 00:15:39,973
PASS YOUR DRIVER'S TEST
THIS TIME.

357
00:15:40,007 --> 00:15:43,377
COULD YOU GET OUT OF THE CAR?

358
00:15:43,410 --> 00:15:44,612
GET GOING.

359
00:15:44,645 --> 00:15:45,945
IT WAS FUN,
I THINK I'M FINALLY

360
00:15:45,978 --> 00:15:47,715
COMING OUT
OF MY DEPRESSION.

361
00:15:49,617 --> 00:15:51,952
THE DEATH RAY'S JUST
RATTLING AROUND THE TRUNK.

362
00:15:51,985 --> 00:15:53,920
HOPE THEY WRAPPED
A BLANKET AROUND IT.

363
00:15:56,223 --> 00:15:57,892
THERE'S A DARKNESS
AT THE EDGE OF EUROPE.

364
00:16:01,595 --> 00:16:03,197
AH, RIGHT, LEAVE
JUST ENOUGH ROOM

365
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:04,932
FOR THEM TO GET THROUGH.

366
00:16:08,635 --> 00:16:11,105
- [ALL LAUGH]
- THERE, WE MADE THEM
SWERVE SLIGHTLY.

367
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:17,177
WHOA, SULLY'S GONNA
BLOW GROCERIES.

368
00:16:17,210 --> 00:16:21,013
STOP AT WALGREENS,
WILL YOU?

369
00:16:21,047 --> 00:16:22,482
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

370
00:16:22,515 --> 00:16:24,418
PASS IF YOU'RE GONNA.

371
00:16:35,628 --> 00:16:37,563
JEEZ, FELLAS, IF WE
ONLY HAD A DEATH RAY,

372
00:16:37,597 --> 00:16:39,733
WE COULD-- HEY!

373
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:45,338
THIS IS SO LUCKY,
WE NEEDED A HELICOPTER!

374
00:16:45,372 --> 00:16:46,607
IT'S TOM WOLFE!

375
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:51,745
CAN YOU IMAGINE
THE HORRIBLE KINDS OF PEACE

376
00:16:51,778 --> 00:16:55,282
THE BAD GUYS WILL WAGE
WITH THAT DEATH RAY?

377
00:16:55,315 --> 00:16:57,650
I'M NOT THAT DRUNK,
LET ME GO, I CAN FLY IT.

378
00:17:02,022 --> 00:17:04,257
THE CHAUFFEUR'S NOT
GONNA GET HIS TIP NOW.

379
00:17:08,562 --> 00:17:11,098
WOW, CHAUFFEURS ARE
DOING IT FOR THEMSELVES.

380
00:17:14,702 --> 00:17:17,437
GET THIS TOY
OUT OF HERE, QUICK.

381
00:17:21,742 --> 00:17:23,577
HELLO, HELLO, HEADQUARTERS?

382
00:17:23,610 --> 00:17:24,678
THEY'RE ESCAPING
IN A HELICOPTER.

383
00:17:24,712 --> 00:17:26,213
AND IT'S COOL!

384
00:17:26,247 --> 00:17:27,613
SO STUPID.

385
00:17:35,088 --> 00:17:37,623
THIS IS MY FAVORITE PART
OF MY JOB.

386
00:17:39,493 --> 00:17:41,262
QUICK, LET'S RUN FOR IT.

387
00:17:45,032 --> 00:17:47,300
OH, THAT ONE SPOT ON MY BACK,
I CAN'T REACH IT.

388
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:51,938
RIBBIT.

389
00:17:51,972 --> 00:17:55,108
HONEST-TO-GOODNESS REAL,
NOT TOY, HELICOPTER.

390
00:17:55,142 --> 00:17:57,143
ANYBODY BRING THE DEATH RAY?

391
00:17:57,177 --> 00:17:58,245
ATTENTION, HEADQUARTERS.

392
00:17:58,278 --> 00:17:59,847
THEIR DIRECTION
IS SOUTHWEST.

393
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,248
THE CHOPPER IS PAINTED WHITE
AND RED AND HAS A BLUE TAIL.

394
00:18:02,282 --> 00:18:05,052
- OVER AND OUT.
- ATTENTION ALL
AIRPORT PATROLS.

395
00:18:05,085 --> 00:18:08,022
WATCH OUT FOR A SINGLE-BLADE
HELICOPTER HEADING SOUTHWEST.

396
00:18:08,055 --> 00:18:10,790
THEY HAVE A KIDNAPPED SCIENTIST
WITH THEM ONBOARD.

397
00:18:10,823 --> 00:18:14,695
- [HARP MUSIC]
- NOW WE'RE IN HEAVEN.

398
00:18:14,728 --> 00:18:17,832
TIDY-BOWL MAN IS DOING
ALL RIGHT FOR HIMSELF.

399
00:18:17,865 --> 00:18:20,000
THEY'RE COMING UP FOR
MORE BAKING SODA.

400
00:18:24,672 --> 00:18:27,473
AHH, THE OCEAN'S BEAUTIFUL
IN THIS PART OF THE TUB.

401
00:18:30,143 --> 00:18:32,478
THIS SET IS AT LEAST
THREE BOX TOPS.

402
00:18:32,512 --> 00:18:36,217
SPECIAL EFFECTS BY BILLY!

403
00:18:36,250 --> 00:18:38,352
THESE ARE NOT TOYS.

404
00:18:44,023 --> 00:18:46,227
A WILLOWY SUB COMMANDER.

405
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:49,963
SO WHEN DOES THE MUMMENSCHANZ
REHEARSAL START?

406
00:18:49,997 --> 00:18:52,065
DON'T GO UP THERE,
YOU'LL BECOME A TOY.

407
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:56,002
YA-HOW!

408
00:18:56,035 --> 00:18:57,703
THANK YOU,
EASTMAN WIDESCREEN.

409
00:19:03,210 --> 00:19:05,845
WHY HAVE YOU TAKEN ME
TO THE PETERSONS BATHROOM?

410
00:19:09,182 --> 00:19:11,017
THIS IS SO INDULGENT.

411
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:17,823
UNDERALLS FOR MEN.

412
00:19:17,857 --> 00:19:19,793
OKAY, SO MY DEATH RAY
PRESENTATION

413
00:19:19,827 --> 00:19:23,563
WASN'T THAT SNAPPY.

414
00:19:23,597 --> 00:19:25,465
OW.

415
00:19:25,498 --> 00:19:26,967
DANGER! TWIST TIE.

416
00:19:31,438 --> 00:19:33,473
AND MORE BUTTS.

417
00:19:33,507 --> 00:19:35,942
OH, NOW HE'S SHOWBOATING
HIS BUTT.

418
00:19:44,483 --> 00:19:46,653
OKAY, WE CAN DIVE.

419
00:19:46,687 --> 00:19:49,422
BILLY'S OUT OF THE TUB,
WE CAN DIVE.

420
00:19:49,455 --> 00:19:51,558
HEAD TOWARDS THE DRAIN.

421
00:19:51,592 --> 00:19:54,628
DAS TOYBOAT.

422
00:19:54,662 --> 00:19:57,030
COULD SOMEBODY TIE ON
THE HELICOPTER?

423
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:01,568
OH, THIS MUST BE
A MASSIVE ORGANIZATION

424
00:20:01,602 --> 00:20:03,970
TO BE ABLE TO THROW AWAY
A $1.50 HELICOPTER.

425
00:20:08,042 --> 00:20:09,743
ADORN.

426
00:20:15,082 --> 00:20:17,183
OH, WELL, THEY'D BETTER
LET THE TUB COOL DOWN

427
00:20:17,217 --> 00:20:19,887
BEFORE THEY USE IT NOW.

428
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:23,523
YOU'RE HERE, BUT SHE'S HERE
WITH THE TRAVELER'S CHECKS.

429
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:27,593
AH, VERY NICE.

430
00:20:32,632 --> 00:20:34,868
VAGUELY EUROPEAN GIGOLO.

431
00:20:34,902 --> 00:20:36,737
DRINK ME IN, FOLKS.

432
00:20:43,377 --> 00:20:46,413
- BING.
- BAH-BADA-BA-DADA.

433
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:49,415
HOT HOUSEKEEPING.

434
00:20:51,718 --> 00:20:54,487
THEY'VE GOT SATELLITE DISHES
ON THEIR EARS.

435
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:02,795
CHECK-OUT'S NOT TILL TEN!

436
00:21:02,828 --> 00:21:04,497
WHAT A PLEASANT SURPRISE.

437
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:05,598
WHAT THE HELL DO YOU WANT?

438
00:21:05,632 --> 00:21:07,667
THE BOSS WOULD LIKE
TO SEE YOU.

439
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,970
YOU'RE JOKING, I ONLY
JUST COMPLETED A JOB.

440
00:21:10,003 --> 00:21:11,805
HAVEN'T HAD ANY SLEEP
FOR THREE NIGHTS.

441
00:21:11,838 --> 00:21:14,908
- YOU KNOW THAT.
- IT'S URGENT, MR. FARGO.

442
00:21:14,942 --> 00:21:17,510
VERY URGENT.

443
00:21:17,543 --> 00:21:19,647
JETHRO!

444
00:21:21,047 --> 00:21:24,752
WE'VE GOTTA GET DRUNK,
IT'S URGENT.

445
00:21:24,785 --> 00:21:27,287
WELL, I'M GLAD TO SAY
THAT OUR CLIENTS

446
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:29,923
WERE VERY PLEASED,
YES, WELL DONE.

447
00:21:29,957 --> 00:21:32,358
YOU DESERVE A SPECIAL PRIZE
FOR YOUR WORK.

448
00:21:32,392 --> 00:21:34,493
HE'S WON THE IRVING
THALBERG AWARD.

449
00:21:34,527 --> 00:21:38,432
ANOTHER JOB, AND ONE
OF INTERNATIONAL IMPORTANCE,

450
00:21:38,465 --> 00:21:40,667
THE NATO AUTHORITIES
HAVE ENLISTED

451
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:42,902
THE HELP OF OUR
ORGANIZATION

452
00:21:42,935 --> 00:21:45,572
IN TRACING A KIDNAPPED
RESEARCH SCIENTIST.

453
00:21:45,605 --> 00:21:46,873
EXCUSE ME, SENOR RAYMOND,
BUT YOU--

454
00:21:46,907 --> 00:21:48,975
OH, DO WE HAVE TO GO
THROUGH ALL THAT AGAIN?

455
00:21:49,008 --> 00:21:51,512
YOU'LL GET YOUR
USUAL PAY AND A BONUS.

456
00:21:51,545 --> 00:21:53,413
SO DON'T TRY TO ARGUE
ABOUT IT NOW.

457
00:21:53,447 --> 00:21:55,715
IT WON'T DO ANY GOOD.

458
00:21:55,748 --> 00:21:56,817
YOU ARE WORSE THAN AN ARAB.

459
00:21:56,850 --> 00:21:58,385
OH, COME ON!

460
00:21:58,418 --> 00:22:00,153
--HOW MUCH YOU'RE GOING
TO COLLECT ON A JOB.

461
00:22:00,187 --> 00:22:01,455
IF YOU HADN'T
SUCH A GOOD RECORD,

462
00:22:01,488 --> 00:22:02,955
I WOULD HAVE GOT
RID OF YOU ALREADY.

463
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:04,290
- I'M SORRY.
- THE NEW CASE

464
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:07,527
IS A MATTER OF LIFE AND DEATH
FOR THE WHOLE WORLD.

465
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:08,962
SENOR RAYMOND,

466
00:22:08,995 --> 00:22:10,797
CAN'T YOU USE ANYONE ELSE
IN THIS JOB?

467
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:12,865
- ONE OF THE INTERNS.
- JUST WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

468
00:22:12,898 --> 00:22:15,302
YOU SEE, I'M ON HOLIDAY.

469
00:22:15,335 --> 00:22:17,003
DON'T YOU REMEMBER?

470
00:22:17,037 --> 00:22:19,372
YOU PROMISED ME I COULD TAKE
TWO WEEKS VACATION AFTER I--

471
00:22:19,405 --> 00:22:20,973
DON'T WORRY,
DO THIS JOB WELL,

472
00:22:21,007 --> 00:22:23,277
AND I'LL GIVE YOU
A MONTH'S VACATION.

473
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:25,312
THERE IS ALL THE INFORMATION
YOU MAY NEED.

474
00:22:25,345 --> 00:22:26,713
IN THE DOSSIER OUT THERE.

475
00:22:26,747 --> 00:22:28,248
MY SECRETARY WILL
GIVE IT TO YOU.

476
00:22:28,282 --> 00:22:29,648
DON'T FORGET,
IT'S TOP SECRET.

477
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:32,252
READ IT,
AND THEN DESTROY IT.

478
00:22:32,285 --> 00:22:33,520
IS THAT CLEAR, FARGO?

479
00:22:33,553 --> 00:22:34,687
YEAH, EVERYTHING'S CLEAR.

480
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:36,757
IT'S CLEAR THIS
IS BOGUS, MAN.

481
00:22:36,790 --> 00:22:38,725
ONE LAST THING.
AS USUAL, I EXPECT

482
00:22:38,758 --> 00:22:40,693
REPORTS OVER TIME, FARGO.

483
00:22:40,727 --> 00:22:43,630
USE YOUR MICROTRANSMITTER
ON THE 20-CYCLE BAND.

484
00:22:43,663 --> 00:22:44,730
YEAH.

485
00:22:44,763 --> 00:22:45,965
AND DON'T FORGET.

486
00:22:45,998 --> 00:22:48,502
PROFESSOR JOHN CARMICHAEL'S
DISAPPEARANCE

487
00:22:48,535 --> 00:22:50,803
MULTIPLIES THE RISK
OF A WORLDWIDE CATACLYSM.

488
00:22:50,837 --> 00:22:53,940
AND THAT'S WHY I'VE BEEN HIRED
TO GO AND BRING HIM HERE.

489
00:22:53,973 --> 00:22:55,475
- YEAH, I GET YOU.
- YEAH, FINE,

490
00:22:55,508 --> 00:22:57,943
I'LL SAVE THE WORLD
WHEN I'M READY.

491
00:22:57,977 --> 00:23:00,113
I'M GOING TO FINISH
HIS SCOTCH.

492
00:23:05,318 --> 00:23:06,720
WELL, THAT DOES IT.

493
00:23:06,753 --> 00:23:08,755
TIME FOR MY OBLIGATORY
FLIRTING SCENE.

494
00:23:08,788 --> 00:23:10,223
I'M SORRY, HONEY.

495
00:23:10,257 --> 00:23:12,825
OUR TRIP TO MAJORCA IS OFF.

496
00:23:12,858 --> 00:23:15,962
THE BOSS WAS KIND ENOUGH
TO GIVE ME A NEW ASSIGNMENT.

497
00:23:15,995 --> 00:23:17,263
YES, SO I HEARD,
BUT I THINK

498
00:23:17,297 --> 00:23:18,898
YOU SHOULD HAVE INSISTED
A LITTLE MORE.

499
00:23:18,932 --> 00:23:20,700
YOU KNOW YOU MUST
TAKE A VACATION.

500
00:23:20,733 --> 00:23:22,568
MM, I LIKE IT WHEN
YOU WORRY ABOUT ME.

501
00:23:22,602 --> 00:23:23,803
STRESS TURNS ME ON.

502
00:23:23,837 --> 00:23:24,905
IS THIS THE DOSSIER?

503
00:23:24,938 --> 00:23:26,438
YES, THAT'S THE DOSSIER,
TOP SECRET.

504
00:23:26,472 --> 00:23:28,107
I FOUND IT LAYING AROUND.

505
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:31,778
I HAVE TO GO UNDERCOVER
AS TONY ROBERTS?

506
00:23:31,812 --> 00:23:34,848
OH, DARLING,
TAKE CARE OF YOURSELF.

507
00:23:34,882 --> 00:23:37,750
AND NO FIGHTING
THIS TIME, HUH?

508
00:23:37,783 --> 00:23:39,953
- I DON'T WANT YOU TO DIE.
- UGH, A FERENGI EAR.

509
00:23:39,987 --> 00:23:42,588
THE OTHER GUYS USUALLY
NEED PLASTIC SURGERY.

510
00:23:42,622 --> 00:23:44,825
ANYWAY, WHEN I GET BACK,
WE'LL GO TO MAJORCA FOR A MONTH.

511
00:23:44,858 --> 00:23:46,258
HIS PHONE HAS LOST WEIGHT.

512
00:23:46,292 --> 00:23:48,295
BUT DON'T LEAVE
TILL TOMORROW.

513
00:23:48,328 --> 00:23:50,297
SPEND THE NIGHT WITH ME.

514
00:23:50,330 --> 00:23:51,732
EH, LORETO ROBERTA!

515
00:23:51,765 --> 00:23:53,065
- GET BACK TO WORK.
- D'OH!

516
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:54,700
MUST I REMIND YOU AGAIN?

517
00:23:54,733 --> 00:23:56,202
NOT TO DISTRACT OUR AGENTS.

518
00:23:56,235 --> 00:23:57,670
AND FARGO, YOU ARE
TO LEAVE AT ONCE.

519
00:23:57,703 --> 00:23:59,005
DO YOU HEAR THAT? AT ONCE.

520
00:23:59,038 --> 00:24:00,940
I'M TRYING TO RUN AN
INTERNATIONAL ORGANIZATION,

521
00:24:00,973 --> 00:24:03,877
AND YOU GUYS ARE BUGGING ME.

522
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:06,312
AND REMEMBER. MAJORCA.

523
00:24:06,345 --> 00:24:09,282
SELLING VINYL SIDING
IS FULL OF INTRIGUE.

524
00:24:22,728 --> 00:24:24,530
BAH-BADA-BA-DADA.

525
00:24:24,563 --> 00:24:26,232
AAH! SERVO, WHAT IS THAT?

526
00:24:26,265 --> 00:24:28,067
OH, MIKE.
IT'S A DEATH RAY I MADE.

527
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:29,468
DEATH RAY?

528
00:24:29,502 --> 00:24:31,938
YEAH, BUT, OF COURSE, I MADE IT
FOR PEACEFUL PURPOSES ONLY.

529
00:24:31,972 --> 00:24:33,973
I CO-- OH, WAIT,
HERE COMES CROW.

530
00:24:34,007 --> 00:24:36,475
OH JEEZ, I KNOW I MADE IT
FOR PEACEFUL PURPOSES ONLY,

531
00:24:36,508 --> 00:24:38,010
BUT I JUST CAN'T RESIST!

532
00:24:38,043 --> 00:24:40,747
SERVO, NO!

533
00:24:43,850 --> 00:24:46,018
WHAT THE HECK
WAS THAT FOR?

534
00:24:46,052 --> 00:24:48,355
OH BOY, I'M SORRY,
THAT WAS MY DEATH RAY.

535
00:24:48,388 --> 00:24:51,190
I HAD INTENDED IT TO BE
FOR PEACEFUL PURPOSES ONLY.

536
00:24:51,223 --> 00:24:54,093
BUT THEN YOU CAME ALONG,
AND-- [LAUGHS]

537
00:24:54,127 --> 00:24:57,297
I GOTTA ADMIT,
IT IS PRETTY FUNNY.

538
00:25:04,137 --> 00:25:06,807
[CROW SCREAMS]

539
00:25:19,352 --> 00:25:20,520
OH, IT IS A DANGEROUS
MISSION.

540
00:25:20,553 --> 00:25:22,788
IT'S U.S. AIR.

541
00:25:26,325 --> 00:25:28,362
[ALL SING]

542
00:25:28,395 --> 00:25:29,728
--ENGLISH FIRM.

543
00:25:29,762 --> 00:25:32,032
AND THE COMMERCIAL RELATIONS
BETWEEN ENGLAND AND FRANCE

544
00:25:32,065 --> 00:25:34,467
AREN'T ALWAYS EASY,
AND YOU KNOW WHY?

545
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:36,035
'CAUSE THE FROGS
DON'T LISTEN.

546
00:25:36,068 --> 00:25:37,637
--BOTH COUNTRIES ARE TRYING
TO SELL THE SAME PRODUCTS

547
00:25:37,670 --> 00:25:39,605
- TO EACH OTHER.
- COULD YOU NOT TALK?

548
00:25:39,638 --> 00:25:41,373
--THAT, WELL...

549
00:25:41,407 --> 00:25:43,343
ARE YOU FEELING
ALL RIGHT NOW, SENORA?

550
00:25:43,377 --> 00:25:45,945
I DON'T KNOW.

551
00:25:45,978 --> 00:25:47,913
MONSIEUR, YOU WERE SAYING.

552
00:25:47,947 --> 00:25:50,317
- CONTINUE YOUR STORY.
- WHAT?

553
00:25:50,350 --> 00:25:51,652
OH, NO, SHE'S PRETTIER
THAN YOU.

554
00:25:51,685 --> 00:25:53,553
OH, I'VE ALREADY
BORED YOU WITH IT.

555
00:25:53,587 --> 00:25:54,853
LET'S TALK ABOUT YOU.

556
00:25:54,887 --> 00:25:56,422
- WHAT DO YOU DO?
- I'M BEAUTIFUL.

557
00:25:56,455 --> 00:25:58,758
WELL, MY WORK ISN'T
PARTICULARLY INTERESTING.

558
00:25:58,792 --> 00:26:00,960
AS A FASHION EDITOR,
I'M JUST LIKE YOU.

559
00:26:00,993 --> 00:26:02,362
CONTINUALLY TRAVELING.

560
00:26:02,395 --> 00:26:04,730
BUT ONCE ONE GETS
USED TO IT, LUCKILY.

561
00:26:04,763 --> 00:26:05,898
DANGER! SMALL TALK.

562
00:26:05,932 --> 00:26:08,100
SO WHERE ARE YOU
BOUND FOR THIS TIME?

563
00:26:08,133 --> 00:26:09,535
A SHORT VISIT TO THE EAST.

564
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:11,203
- NEW JERSEY?
- AND YOU?

565
00:26:11,237 --> 00:26:12,838
TO THE WEST.

566
00:26:12,872 --> 00:26:14,173
WHAT A PITY.

567
00:26:14,207 --> 00:26:15,442
AW.

568
00:26:15,475 --> 00:26:17,243
THAT MEANS WE CAN'T BOINK.

569
00:26:19,178 --> 00:26:22,382
MEANWHILE, IN COACH.

570
00:26:22,415 --> 00:26:26,085
WELCOME TO STRUCTURE.

571
00:26:26,118 --> 00:26:28,053
HERE I AM, IN THE WEST.

572
00:26:28,087 --> 00:26:29,688
THE WEST IS NICE.

573
00:26:31,958 --> 00:26:33,527
[SERVO RETCHES]

574
00:26:36,062 --> 00:26:39,232
DIDN'T KNOW MY YOUTH HOSTEL
LOCKED THE DOOR AT 10:00.

575
00:26:41,735 --> 00:26:44,303
NOT WITHOUT MY DAUGHTER.

576
00:26:44,337 --> 00:26:48,007
DOUG FAIRBANKS
COMES HOME LATE.

577
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:51,510
MM, I THINK HE MISSED THIS DAY
IN SECRET AGENT TRAINING.

578
00:26:51,543 --> 00:26:53,547
I THINK HE WORE
THE WRONG SHOES.

579
00:26:56,215 --> 00:26:58,985
OLLIE NORTH ARRIVES
AT CAMPAIGN HEADQUARTERS.

580
00:27:05,192 --> 00:27:07,527
THAT WAS REALLY HIM.

581
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:10,197
YOU OUGHTA CLEAN THE POOL,
IT'S FILTHY.

582
00:27:13,198 --> 00:27:15,135
AUGUSTUS HAS FALLEN
INTO THE CHOCOLATE!

583
00:27:17,503 --> 00:27:19,705
HEY, SOMEBODY TELL
THE DIRECTOR WE LOST HIM.

584
00:27:19,738 --> 00:27:21,407
I THINK HE'S DEAD.

585
00:27:24,477 --> 00:27:26,212
SURE, WE GOT A LITTLE
WATER IN THE BASEMENT,

586
00:27:26,245 --> 00:27:27,580
WHAT OF IT?

587
00:27:30,717 --> 00:27:33,185
[CROW GASPS, COUGHS]

588
00:27:33,218 --> 00:27:35,655
MOMMY, I SWAM ALL THE WAY
OUT TO THE RAFT.

589
00:27:37,390 --> 00:27:39,158
WHAT THE HELL
AM I DOING HERE?

590
00:27:41,593 --> 00:27:43,763
WILL MARCIA FIND LOVE?

591
00:27:43,797 --> 00:27:46,933
WILL DR. DRESSEN FIND
A CURE FOR DANNY?

592
00:27:49,068 --> 00:27:51,938
IT'S LIKE WHEN RATS POP OUT
OF THE TOILETS IN ST. PAUL.

593
00:27:53,138 --> 00:27:55,575
IT'S SO EMBARRASSING.

594
00:27:57,243 --> 00:27:58,377
HEY, MARIO, WHAT
TOOK YOU SO LONG?

595
00:27:58,410 --> 00:27:59,978
LOOKS LIKE A TALL ELF.

596
00:28:00,012 --> 00:28:01,580
I JUST GOT A MESSAGE
FROM THE BOSS.

597
00:28:01,613 --> 00:28:03,617
HE SAID TO EXPECT A VISITOR,

598
00:28:03,650 --> 00:28:05,385
SOMEONE'S LOOKING
FOR THE SPANIARD.

599
00:28:05,418 --> 00:28:06,585
WHERE IS SCARFACE?

600
00:28:06,618 --> 00:28:08,053
THAT'S MY AFFAIR.

601
00:28:08,087 --> 00:28:09,388
YOU JUST CARRY OUT ORDERS.

602
00:28:09,422 --> 00:28:11,557
A CHARLIE WATTS WALK-ON.

603
00:28:15,295 --> 00:28:17,063
WELL, YOU LEAVE YOURSELF OPEN
TO THIS KIND OF THING

604
00:28:17,097 --> 00:28:19,498
WHEN YOU HAVE A TRAP DOOR.

605
00:28:28,273 --> 00:28:30,577
WHEN STUNTMEN
TRY TO PLAY CARDS.

606
00:28:30,610 --> 00:28:32,045
SIX, NO HEARTS!

607
00:28:35,013 --> 00:28:37,217
I HATE TRIPLE SEC!

608
00:28:39,318 --> 00:28:41,855
COME ON, FATSO.

609
00:28:41,888 --> 00:28:45,725
I JUST HAD A HENNA RINSE.

610
00:28:45,758 --> 00:28:47,893
YOU'RE SUCH A BONER, MAN.

611
00:28:54,033 --> 00:28:56,535
OH, THIS IS THE BEST
FORTUNE HUNTER YET!

612
00:28:58,572 --> 00:28:59,905
D'OH!

613
00:29:05,912 --> 00:29:07,447
YOU'RE THE ONE THAT
KNOWS EVERYTHING.

614
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:09,248
- WHO'S GOD?
- WHERE'S THE MAN
WITH THE SCAR?

615
00:29:09,282 --> 00:29:11,250
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN!

616
00:29:11,283 --> 00:29:13,085
YOU'D BETTER TALK!

617
00:29:13,118 --> 00:29:15,188
- WHERE IS HE?
- I'M TRYING--
- PLEASE.

618
00:29:15,222 --> 00:29:16,622
SURE, I'LL TALK.

619
00:29:16,655 --> 00:29:17,957
- BUT DON'T--
- LET GO OF MY LARYNX.

620
00:29:17,990 --> 00:29:19,958
SCARFACE ISN'T HERE
IN ROME.

621
00:29:19,992 --> 00:29:22,228
HE LEFT TWO DAYS AGO.

622
00:29:22,262 --> 00:29:24,063
THE BOSS ORDERED HIM
TO LEAVE.

623
00:29:24,097 --> 00:29:26,432
- HE WENT TO--
- HA-HA.

624
00:29:29,902 --> 00:29:32,972
♪ DID YOU EVER HAVE
TO MAKE UP YOUR MIND ♪

625
00:29:34,907 --> 00:29:36,308
WE'RE GONNA GET DOWN NOW,

626
00:29:36,342 --> 00:29:38,878
'CAUSE THERE'S A FUNKY KIND
OF INTRIGUE GOING ON.

627
00:29:44,117 --> 00:29:45,518
I JUST WANTED TO THANK YOU!

628
00:29:45,552 --> 00:29:47,553
THANK YOU FOR
KILLING THAT GUY!

629
00:29:51,557 --> 00:29:54,293
♪ WATERMELON MAN ♪

630
00:29:56,662 --> 00:29:59,665
THESE SANSABELTS ARE
MADE FOR ACTION.

631
00:29:59,698 --> 00:30:01,600
I'LL WAIT FOR YOU HERE
FOR A LITTLE WHILE.

632
00:30:05,338 --> 00:30:07,507
I'M COUNTING ON HIM
BEING COMPLETELY BLIND.

633
00:30:09,475 --> 00:30:12,078
JACK LELANE
IS THE FUGITIVE.

634
00:30:13,880 --> 00:30:16,182
♪ WATERMELON MAN ♪

635
00:30:19,352 --> 00:30:20,820
I REFUSE TO LOOK
TO THE RIGHT.

636
00:30:20,853 --> 00:30:22,422
IT WOULD BE CAVING IN
TO LOOK THAT WAY.

637
00:30:22,455 --> 00:30:24,257
I WILL NOT.

638
00:30:24,290 --> 00:30:26,425
WELL, I TRIED MY BEST,
THAT'S ALL THEY CAN ASK.

639
00:30:26,458 --> 00:30:29,128
I AM TECHNICALLY
ON VACATION.

640
00:30:29,162 --> 00:30:31,330
KIND OF A HASTILY
ASSEMBLED RUIN.

641
00:30:35,935 --> 00:30:38,203
OH, GROSS, HE'S WEARING
A SPORTS BRA!

642
00:30:40,340 --> 00:30:41,840
THAT WAS KIND OF A LET-DOWN.

643
00:30:41,873 --> 00:30:43,275
I WAS EXPECTING
A BETTER CHASE.

644
00:30:43,308 --> 00:30:45,278
NOW I'VE GOT THE WHOLE
REST OF THE EVENING.

645
00:30:48,615 --> 00:30:50,883
OOF, WHY THE HELL
DID I GO DOWN THERE?

646
00:30:50,917 --> 00:30:54,387
WHAT WAS I THINKING OF?

647
00:30:54,420 --> 00:30:56,455
OOH, SOMEBODY'S WET.

648
00:30:59,992 --> 00:31:02,695
♪ WATERMELON MAN ♪

649
00:31:04,763 --> 00:31:07,767
GROWING NEED FOR SECURITY MEN
IN SEATTLE AREA.

650
00:31:13,707 --> 00:31:16,142
I WAS JUST REACHING
FOR MY MINT!

651
00:31:18,945 --> 00:31:20,647
GROW SOME HAIR.

652
00:31:26,085 --> 00:31:28,655
♪ WATERMELON MAN ♪

653
00:31:30,390 --> 00:31:33,092
LOVE TO SNEAK INTO
MY OWN APARTMENT.

654
00:31:34,860 --> 00:31:37,230
THAT'S HERBIE HANCOCK,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

655
00:31:37,263 --> 00:31:40,600
YES, WE'RE GONNA TAKE
A LITTLE BREAK RIGHT NOW.

656
00:31:40,633 --> 00:31:42,502
KIND OF HARD FOR ME
TO WORK WITHOUT MY MUSIC,

657
00:31:42,535 --> 00:31:43,903
BUT I'LL TRY.

658
00:31:43,937 --> 00:31:46,238
MIGHT AS WELL TAKE A COUPLE
OF LAPS AROUND THE BUILDING.

659
00:31:48,507 --> 00:31:50,577
HELLO? HELLO?

660
00:31:50,610 --> 00:31:51,943
X-3 CALLING.

661
00:31:51,977 --> 00:31:53,312
ARE YOU RECEIVING ME?

662
00:31:53,345 --> 00:31:55,213
ANSWER!

663
00:31:59,352 --> 00:32:00,887
THIS APARTMENT'S RENTED!

664
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:02,855
ATTENTION, ATTENTION.

665
00:32:02,888 --> 00:32:05,157
MICHAEL EISNER
AND JEFFREY KATZENBERG'S

666
00:32:05,190 --> 00:32:06,993
LAST MEETING.

667
00:32:07,027 --> 00:32:10,095
STAND BY FOR
IMPORTANT MESSAGE.

668
00:32:10,128 --> 00:32:12,798
ARE YOU RECEIVING US?
COME IN?

669
00:32:12,832 --> 00:32:13,933
HEY, YOU'RE COMFORTABLE.

670
00:32:13,967 --> 00:32:16,202
COME IN, X-3.

671
00:32:16,235 --> 00:32:19,005
YES, RECEIVING YOU,
GO AHEAD, OVER.

672
00:32:19,038 --> 00:32:21,340
OKAY, X-3,
I'LL GIVE YOU FRANK.

673
00:32:21,373 --> 00:32:23,208
X-3, HOW ARE YOU?

674
00:32:23,242 --> 00:32:25,678
WE INTEND TO LAND
NEAR BARCELONA IN A FEW HOURS.

675
00:32:25,712 --> 00:32:28,147
- RIBBIT, OVER.
- RENDEZVOUS AT THE
CLUB MOROCCO.

676
00:32:28,180 --> 00:32:30,048
REPEAT, RENDEZVOUS
AT THE CLUB MOROCCO.

677
00:32:30,082 --> 00:32:31,783
- NOSFERATU?
- IS THAT CLEAR?

678
00:32:31,817 --> 00:32:33,452
YES, MESSAGE RECEIVED.

679
00:32:33,485 --> 00:32:35,922
I DON'T HAVE THE RIGHT CLOTHES
FOR THE CLUB MOROCCO.

680
00:32:39,358 --> 00:32:41,160
IT'S A LADY WITTNAUER.

681
00:32:41,193 --> 00:32:43,362
HELLO? FARGO HERE.

682
00:32:43,395 --> 00:32:45,665
HELLO, HOW ARE
THINGS GOING?

683
00:32:45,698 --> 00:32:46,998
FINE, SENOR RAYMOND.

684
00:32:47,032 --> 00:32:48,300
GUESS WHERE
I'M GOING TONIGHT?

685
00:32:48,333 --> 00:32:49,802
JUST MADE SOME NEW FRIENDS.

686
00:32:49,835 --> 00:32:51,437
- I'M SITTING ON ONE RIGHT NOW.
- I'M HEADED TO BARCELONA.

687
00:32:51,470 --> 00:32:53,272
SO TAKE THE USUAL STEPS.

688
00:32:53,305 --> 00:32:54,607
RIGHT, ANYTHING ELSE?

689
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:55,842
YES, SENOR RAYMOND.

690
00:32:55,875 --> 00:32:57,910
WARM WISHES
TO YOUR SECRETARY.

691
00:32:57,943 --> 00:32:59,678
I'M HERE.
BE CAREFUL, BARTON,

692
00:32:59,712 --> 00:33:01,213
- DON'T--
- OVER AND OUT.

693
00:33:01,247 --> 00:33:04,650
NOBODY DOESN'T LIKE ME.

694
00:33:04,683 --> 00:33:06,018
MACINTOSH EQUIPMENT.

695
00:33:06,052 --> 00:33:07,420
MACINTOSH? NICE TUBE AMP.

696
00:33:07,453 --> 00:33:08,587
QUITE QUALITY, YOU MIGHT--

697
00:33:08,620 --> 00:33:09,988
OH, HEY!

698
00:33:18,063 --> 00:33:19,832
ADORN.

699
00:33:22,802 --> 00:33:25,872
JUST A FEW MORE HOURS ON BOARD,
PROFESSOR CARMICHAEL.

700
00:33:25,905 --> 00:33:27,173
AND WE'LL BE MARRIED.

701
00:33:27,207 --> 00:33:28,407
--START RECREATING
YOUR DEATH RAY,

702
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:31,210
NOT FOR NATO BUT FOR
PRIVATE ENTERPRISE.

703
00:33:31,243 --> 00:33:34,047
YOU WILL NEVER MANAGE TO MAKE
ME WORK AGAINST MY WILL.

704
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:36,648
OH WAIT, YOU WILL,
WHAT AM I SAYING?

705
00:33:36,682 --> 00:33:38,283
DANGER! BEER GUT.

706
00:33:38,317 --> 00:33:39,918
X-2 CALLING.

707
00:33:39,952 --> 00:33:41,120
CAN YOU HEAR ME?

708
00:33:41,153 --> 00:33:42,722
CAN YOU HEAR ME?

709
00:33:42,755 --> 00:33:45,357
PROCEED, X-2, OVER.

710
00:33:45,390 --> 00:33:46,925
WHAT'S WRONG?

711
00:33:46,958 --> 00:33:48,293
WHAT'S WRONG, X-2?

712
00:33:48,327 --> 00:33:50,930
- I'M JUST KIND OF DOWN.
- GO AHEAD.

713
00:33:50,963 --> 00:33:52,765
GO AHEAD, WE'RE WAITING
FOR YOUR MESSAGE.

714
00:33:52,798 --> 00:33:54,733
- OVER.
- THIS MOVIE'S PACKED
WITH HINDERS.

715
00:33:54,767 --> 00:33:56,535
X-2, COME IN!

716
00:33:56,568 --> 00:33:58,170
SUNDAY MORNING
AT SKULL AND BONES.

717
00:33:58,203 --> 00:34:00,305
COME IN, X-2!

718
00:34:00,338 --> 00:34:01,873
TONIGHT,

719
00:34:01,907 --> 00:34:03,175
AN AMERICAN

720
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:05,778
TRIED TO FIND X-1.

721
00:34:05,812 --> 00:34:07,547
WE DID OUR BEST TO--

722
00:34:07,580 --> 00:34:09,348
TO PREVENT...

723
00:34:09,382 --> 00:34:11,550
WELL, IT WASN'T GOOD ENOUGH,
WAS IT?

724
00:34:11,583 --> 00:34:14,220
X-2, REPLY IMMEDIATELY!

725
00:34:14,253 --> 00:34:15,955
CAN'T YOU HEAR, X-2,
WHAT'S WRONG?

726
00:34:15,988 --> 00:34:17,923
JUDGING FROM YOUR FACE,

727
00:34:17,957 --> 00:34:20,693
I'M PRETTY CERTAIN THAT
OUR CONCLUSIONS ARE THE SAME.

728
00:34:20,727 --> 00:34:22,093
YOU'RE DAMN UGLY.

729
00:34:22,127 --> 00:34:23,495
HALF AN HOUR AGO,
YOU GAVE AWAY

730
00:34:23,528 --> 00:34:25,330
DETAILS OF YOUR RENDEZVOUS

731
00:34:25,363 --> 00:34:27,633
TO A COMPLETE STRANGER.

732
00:34:29,368 --> 00:34:30,503
KEEP QUIET, YOU!

733
00:34:30,537 --> 00:34:32,138
GO SIT OVER THERE INSTEAD!

734
00:34:32,172 --> 00:34:33,807
THAT'S YOUR PUNISHMENT.

735
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:35,542
SORRY.

736
00:34:35,575 --> 00:34:37,543
MAKE CONTACT WITH X-3 AGAIN.

737
00:34:40,278 --> 00:34:42,080
♪ DOO-DOO DOO DOO DOO ♪

738
00:34:42,113 --> 00:34:43,282
♪ WESTERN UNION ♪

739
00:34:43,315 --> 00:34:45,552
MM-MM, NOT GONNA DO IT.

740
00:34:45,585 --> 00:34:48,753
THE COY CAPTIVE.

741
00:34:48,787 --> 00:34:50,957
MY NOSEWHEEL FEELS MUSHY.

742
00:34:53,458 --> 00:34:56,528
WHOO! WE'RE GOING TO IOWA CITY
TO SEE THE DEAD, MAN!

743
00:35:03,435 --> 00:35:04,770
LINCOLN!

744
00:35:04,803 --> 00:35:08,073
ABE LINCOLN IS TIMECOP!

745
00:35:09,675 --> 00:35:11,477
[JAZZ MUSIC]

746
00:35:11,510 --> 00:35:14,647
YES.

747
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,748
EVERYONE!

748
00:35:16,782 --> 00:35:19,852
♪ BAH-BADA-BA-DADA! ♪

749
00:35:19,885 --> 00:35:21,687
AH, EXOTIC LOCATIONS,

750
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:23,322
LIKE THE SOUTH SIDE
OF CHICAGO.

751
00:35:23,355 --> 00:35:24,990
GARY, INDIANA.

752
00:35:25,023 --> 00:35:27,660
♪ BAH DA DA
CRAPPY PART OF TOWN ♪

753
00:35:27,693 --> 00:35:30,128
I WONDER IF THE WHOLE CITY
CAN HEAR MY THEME SONG.

754
00:35:32,398 --> 00:35:34,067
OKAY, HERE WE GO, READY?

755
00:35:34,100 --> 00:35:37,102
- BING!
- BAH-BADA-BADA
BADA-BAH.

756
00:35:39,472 --> 00:35:42,675
WHERE EAGLES DARE
MOVES DOWNTOWN.

757
00:35:42,708 --> 00:35:44,377
WE'RE GONNA
SLOW IT DOWN NOW.

758
00:35:44,410 --> 00:35:46,912
'CAUSE WE LIKE TO DO
EVERYTHING NICE AND EASY.

759
00:35:46,945 --> 00:35:49,382
THAT'S A POORLY-DESIGNED
SUBWAY.

760
00:35:53,218 --> 00:35:55,955
OH, I CAN'T RUN
WITHOUT MY THEME.

761
00:35:55,988 --> 00:35:58,290
IF THE MUSIC SPEEDS UP A BIT,
I CAN CATCH HER.

762
00:35:59,758 --> 00:36:03,162
QUICK, I NEED TO GET
ON THE TILT-A-WHIRL.

763
00:36:03,195 --> 00:36:06,365
- BING!
- BAH-BADA-BADA
BADA-BAH.

764
00:36:06,398 --> 00:36:09,435
BOY, THAT'S FUN, I CAN'T
GET ENOUGH OF THAT.

765
00:36:09,468 --> 00:36:11,737
WHOA, MY EYES REALLY
RACK-FOCUSED THERE.

766
00:36:13,538 --> 00:36:16,375
HAPPY HOUR ALWAYS WINS OUT.

767
00:36:16,408 --> 00:36:17,877
EITHER HE'S NINE FEET TALL,

768
00:36:17,910 --> 00:36:19,912
OR THAT'S A TINY DOOR.

769
00:36:22,648 --> 00:36:25,517
THIS MAN WILL
COMPETE FOR--

770
00:36:27,085 --> 00:36:29,355
I'M GOING TO SHUN HIM.

771
00:36:34,493 --> 00:36:36,428
MAN, THE MOROCCO CLUB
IS REALLY DISAPPOINTING.

772
00:36:36,462 --> 00:36:39,932
THE OLD DAYS, THEY WOULDN'T
EVEN LET YOU IN THERE.

773
00:36:39,965 --> 00:36:43,168
JEEZ, THIS IS PRACTICALLY
A KARATE SCHOOL ALREADY.

774
00:36:45,603 --> 00:36:48,207
MY FALAFEL READY TO GO?

775
00:36:48,240 --> 00:36:49,742
BECAUSE IT'S MOROCCAN.

776
00:36:49,775 --> 00:36:51,010
IF THERE WERE A LOT
OF PEOPLE HERE,

777
00:36:51,043 --> 00:36:52,345
WOULDN'T THEY ALL BE PHONY?

778
00:36:52,378 --> 00:36:53,545
HI.

779
00:36:53,578 --> 00:36:54,780
ARE YOU HIRING DANCERS?

780
00:36:54,813 --> 00:36:56,482
NOBODY AROUND HERE?

781
00:36:56,515 --> 00:36:59,685
DON'T I COUNT?

782
00:36:59,718 --> 00:37:02,322
WHAT DO YOU WANT, SENOR?

783
00:37:02,355 --> 00:37:03,788
A DOUBLE COINTREAU.

784
00:37:03,822 --> 00:37:05,390
[ALL] EW.

785
00:37:05,423 --> 00:37:06,925
WHY NOT? ME TOO.

786
00:37:06,958 --> 00:37:08,827
FIRST, YOU'RE PAYING
WHAT YOU OWE.

787
00:37:08,860 --> 00:37:12,097
$14,000? OKAY.

788
00:37:12,130 --> 00:37:13,632
THIS IS SUCH A FUN PLACE.

789
00:37:13,665 --> 00:37:15,467
THEY SHOULD MAKE IT
INTO A CHAIN.

790
00:37:18,037 --> 00:37:21,607
WELL, I'M A SECRET AGENT,
YOU NOW.

791
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:22,942
NICE LITTLE PLACE YOU HAVE.

792
00:37:22,975 --> 00:37:24,877
ONE OF THE BEST
IN BARCELONA.

793
00:37:24,910 --> 00:37:27,547
AND THE MOST EXPENSIVE.

794
00:37:27,580 --> 00:37:29,648
YOU ARE DRUNK, SENOR AL,
YOU OUGHT TO GO HOME.

795
00:37:29,682 --> 00:37:30,983
YOUR JOB IS
TO SERVE DRINKS.

796
00:37:31,017 --> 00:37:32,785
I HAVE TO AGREE.

797
00:37:32,818 --> 00:37:35,453
THIS MAN WILL COMPETE FOR--

798
00:37:43,162 --> 00:37:44,497
GO, PAL!

799
00:37:45,832 --> 00:37:48,867
I WAS LED TO BELIEVE
THIS WAS AN APPLEBEES!

800
00:37:52,805 --> 00:37:55,073
EXPLAIN TO ME WHY THEY'RE
CALLED BUFFALO WINGS!

801
00:37:55,107 --> 00:37:56,508
BY THE WAY,
IT'S MY BIRTHDAY.

802
00:37:56,542 --> 00:37:58,510
DON'T I GET
A LITTLE CUPCAKE?

803
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:02,382
IT'S JERRY REED!

804
00:38:02,415 --> 00:38:04,150
- HIT HIM!
- YEAH.

805
00:38:07,085 --> 00:38:08,720
THIS MAN COULD--

806
00:38:08,753 --> 00:38:11,257
OH, I SAW ED AMES
DO THAT ON CARSON.

807
00:38:15,460 --> 00:38:17,697
HEY, JIVE AND POTTER
PERFORMED HERE.

808
00:38:19,598 --> 00:38:21,800
SOMETHING IS NOT CLICKING
WITH THIS BUSINESS.

809
00:38:21,833 --> 00:38:23,768
MANAGEMENT PROBLEMS
OR SOMETHING.

810
00:38:25,872 --> 00:38:28,072
MR. LINCOLN? THANK YOU.

811
00:38:31,143 --> 00:38:33,012
ABE LINCOLN'S A BAD COP
ON THE LOOSE.

812
00:38:37,382 --> 00:38:39,285
AH, THE ANNUAL RUNNING
OF THE SECRET AGENTS

813
00:38:39,318 --> 00:38:41,253
IN PAMPLONA.

814
00:38:45,090 --> 00:38:47,493
AFTER HIM!

815
00:38:47,527 --> 00:38:49,362
HELP ME, KIRK.

816
00:38:49,395 --> 00:38:50,997
- IS IT BAD?
- NO.

817
00:38:51,030 --> 00:38:52,398
OH, OW.

818
00:38:52,432 --> 00:38:53,698
FOLLOW THE AMERICAN.

819
00:38:53,732 --> 00:38:55,133
DON'T LET HIM GET AWAY.

820
00:38:55,167 --> 00:38:56,435
I WANT JEFFERSON DAVIS DEAD!

821
00:38:56,468 --> 00:38:59,772
I WANT HIS CHILDREN DEAD!

822
00:38:59,805 --> 00:39:01,773
SORRY, BARCELONA'S CLOSED.

823
00:39:01,807 --> 00:39:04,343
THAT'S WHY IT'S CALLED
BAR-CELONA.

824
00:39:08,013 --> 00:39:10,315
RIP!

825
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:12,918
TOO BAD THEY CAN'T JUST
SHOOT THROUGH THE BARS.

826
00:39:16,222 --> 00:39:18,490
HEY, THEY JUST WAXED
THAT ROAD, BE CAREFUL.

827
00:39:21,893 --> 00:39:23,462
THIS ACTION SEQUENCE
BROUGHT TO YOU

828
00:39:23,495 --> 00:39:25,798
BY THE STAN KENTON BAND.

829
00:39:25,832 --> 00:39:29,802
HAH, HOO, HAH, HOO!

830
00:39:29,835 --> 00:39:31,903
I'M ON GHOUL, NOW.

831
00:39:35,842 --> 00:39:36,942
WOW.

832
00:39:36,975 --> 00:39:38,743
WE ARE NOT RENTING!

833
00:39:38,777 --> 00:39:40,512
[SERVO SCATS]

834
00:39:42,982 --> 00:39:44,983
THE BAREFOOT
IN THE PARK CAPER.

835
00:39:47,152 --> 00:39:49,955
[SERVO SCATS]

836
00:39:49,988 --> 00:39:51,157
POOR LITTLE GUY.

837
00:39:51,190 --> 00:39:52,825
SECRET AGENTS CAN
CLIMB REALLY GOOD,

838
00:39:52,858 --> 00:39:55,928
BUT THEY HAVE A HARD TIME
COMING BACK DOWN.

839
00:39:55,962 --> 00:39:58,563
[SERVO SCATS]

840
00:39:58,597 --> 00:40:01,333
SENATOR MIKE MANSFIELD
IN HOT PURSUIT.

841
00:40:04,503 --> 00:40:08,340
IT'S KIND OF
ESCHER-ESQUE, ISN'T IT?

842
00:40:08,373 --> 00:40:09,975
I HAD NO PATIENCE
FOR THE ELEVATOR,

843
00:40:10,008 --> 00:40:11,343
BUT I'M REGRETTING IT NOW.

844
00:40:11,377 --> 00:40:12,745
WHAT IS THIS,
MADAME SOUSATZKA'S

845
00:40:12,778 --> 00:40:14,413
APARTMENT BUILDING?

846
00:40:14,447 --> 00:40:16,682
[SERVO SCATS]

847
00:40:23,788 --> 00:40:25,090
OKAY, EVERYBODY.
QUIET NOW.

848
00:40:25,123 --> 00:40:27,292
I THINK HE'S ON HIS WAY.
THIS IS GONNA BE EXCITING.

849
00:40:27,325 --> 00:40:28,527
RIGHT OVER HERE, MIKE.
COME ON.

850
00:40:28,560 --> 00:40:30,863
THERE WE GO.
RIGHT THERE.

851
00:40:30,897 --> 00:40:32,430
OKAY, WHAT'S THIS ALL ABOUT,
ANYWAY?

852
00:40:32,463 --> 00:40:33,665
OH, YOU'LL FIND OUT.

853
00:40:33,698 --> 00:40:35,333
[LAUGHTER]

854
00:40:35,367 --> 00:40:37,570
WHY, HELLO, MIKE.

855
00:40:37,603 --> 00:40:39,003
HI, TOM.

856
00:40:39,037 --> 00:40:40,605
I BET YOU'RE REALLY SURPRISED

857
00:40:40,638 --> 00:40:43,108
TO SEE ME STANDING HERE, EH?

858
00:40:43,142 --> 00:40:44,543
NOT PARTICULARLY.

859
00:40:44,577 --> 00:40:47,412
AREN'T YOU GOING TO ASK ME
WHY I'M HERE?

860
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:48,447
NO.

861
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:50,015
COME ON, MIKE, ASK ME.

862
00:40:50,048 --> 00:40:51,350
OKAY.
WHY ARE YOU HERE?

863
00:40:51,383 --> 00:40:55,120
I'M HERE, MIKE NELSON,
BECAUSE THIS IS YOUR LIFE.

864
00:40:55,153 --> 00:40:57,322
OH, WOW. THAT'S GREAT.

865
00:40:57,355 --> 00:40:59,325
DRY THOSE TEARS OF JOY,
MIKE NELSON,

866
00:40:59,358 --> 00:41:01,393
BECAUSE YOU'RE ABOUT
TO HEAR THE VOICE

867
00:41:01,427 --> 00:41:03,328
OF A VERY SPECIAL PERSON--

868
00:41:03,362 --> 00:41:06,332
A PERSON WITH WHOM YOU'VE
SHARED MANY GOLDEN MOMENTS.

869
00:41:06,365 --> 00:41:07,365
LET'S LISTEN.

870
00:41:07,398 --> 00:41:08,900
[CROW]
HI, MIKE. HOW YA DOIN'?

871
00:41:08,933 --> 00:41:10,435
DO YOU RECOGNIZE
THAT VOICE, MIKE?

872
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:12,370
YEAH, IT'S CROW.
I MEAN, YOU KNOW...

873
00:41:12,403 --> 00:41:13,805
WELL, THAT'S AMAZING.

874
00:41:13,838 --> 00:41:16,442
YOU STILL RECOGNIZE THE VOICE
OF YOUR DEAR, OLD FRIEND.

875
00:41:16,475 --> 00:41:17,843
I JUST SAW HIM.

876
00:41:17,877 --> 00:41:19,212
BUT WAIT, MIKE.

877
00:41:19,245 --> 00:41:20,545
THERE'S LOTS MORE SURPRISES

878
00:41:20,578 --> 00:41:22,180
ON THIS UNFORGETTABLE EVENING.

879
00:41:22,213 --> 00:41:25,050
DO YOU BY ANY CHANCE
REMEMBER THIS GUY?

880
00:41:25,083 --> 00:41:26,618
[CROW]
HI, MIKE. HOW YA DOIN'?

881
00:41:26,652 --> 00:41:28,587
I WAS DOING FINE, YEAH.

882
00:41:28,620 --> 00:41:30,688
AND THOSE BELOVED MEMORIES
JUST KEEP FLOODING BACK.

883
00:41:30,722 --> 00:41:32,658
NOW WHO COULD FORGET
THIS BELOVED PAL

884
00:41:32,692 --> 00:41:35,327
FROM THOSE CHERISHED,
BYGONE DAYS OF YORE?

885
00:41:35,360 --> 00:41:36,662
[CROW]
HI, MIKE. HOW YA DOIN'?

886
00:41:36,695 --> 00:41:38,097
UH, TOM?

887
00:41:38,130 --> 00:41:40,798
THIS MUST BE A VERY EMOTIONAL
EVENING FOR YOU, MIKE, EH?

888
00:41:40,832 --> 00:41:43,568
TOM, DID YOU EVEN TRY
TO CONTACT ANYBODY ELSE?

889
00:41:43,602 --> 00:41:45,070
LIKE WHO DO YOU MEAN?

890
00:41:45,103 --> 00:41:47,105
I DON'T KNOW.
MY OLD GIRLFRIEND
FROM HIGH SCHOOL.

891
00:41:47,138 --> 00:41:48,340
[CROW]
HI, MIKE. HOW YA DOIN'?

892
00:41:48,373 --> 00:41:50,208
MY TEACHERS, MY PARENTS?

893
00:41:50,242 --> 00:41:51,843
HEY, THOSE ARE REALLY
GOOD IDEAS, MIKE.

894
00:41:51,877 --> 00:41:55,680
BUT WAIT.
HERE COMES YOUR OLD,
DEAR PAL CROW "T" ROBOT.

895
00:41:55,713 --> 00:41:57,315
HI, MIKE! HOW YA DOIN'!

896
00:41:57,348 --> 00:41:58,350
[LAUGHTER]

897
00:41:58,383 --> 00:41:59,452
YOU KNOW, AND RALPH EDWARDS

898
00:41:59,485 --> 00:42:01,220
USED TO GIVE
THESE CHARM BRACELETS

899
00:42:01,253 --> 00:42:03,155
TO COMMEMORATE THE EVENING?

900
00:42:03,188 --> 00:42:04,357
RALPH EDWARDS.

901
00:42:04,390 --> 00:42:05,557
YOU KNOW,
THAT'S A REALLY GOOD IDEA.

902
00:42:05,590 --> 00:42:07,125
YOU SHOULD BUY
ONE OF THEM THERE, MIKE.

903
00:42:07,158 --> 00:42:11,330
BECAUSE, MIKE NELSON,
THIS WAS YOUR LIFE!

904
00:42:11,363 --> 00:42:12,865
NEXT WEEK, ANGIE DICKINSON,

905
00:42:12,898 --> 00:42:15,767
BUT UNTIL THEN,
I'M TOM SERVO...

906
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:17,603
AND CROW "T" ROBOT SAYING...

907
00:42:17,637 --> 00:42:18,770
[ALARM BEEPING]

908
00:42:18,803 --> 00:42:21,040
[BOTH]
THIS IS YOUR--
MOVIE TIME!

909
00:42:37,990 --> 00:42:38,990
HA HA, MIKE.

910
00:42:39,023 --> 00:42:40,993
THAT WAS SWEET.
THANK YOU.

911
00:42:41,027 --> 00:42:43,162
JEEZ. CAN'T HE EVER
USE THE DOOR?

912
00:42:43,195 --> 00:42:46,832
DON'T TELL ME YOU'VE NEVER
BEEN IN AN ARTIST'S STUDIO.

913
00:42:46,865 --> 00:42:49,067
UH-UH. NOT THIS WAY.

914
00:42:49,100 --> 00:42:51,637
UH, ARE YOU LOOKING
FOR SOMEONE?

915
00:42:51,670 --> 00:42:54,238
OH, NO. I JUST LIKE
RUNNING AROUND THE ROOFS.

916
00:42:54,272 --> 00:42:55,607
IT KIND OF RELAXES ME.

917
00:42:55,640 --> 00:42:56,908
DO YOU MIND IF I DROP IN?

918
00:42:56,942 --> 00:42:58,343
PLEASE DO.

919
00:42:58,377 --> 00:43:00,345
I WAS HOPING YOU WOULDN'T
USE THAT JOKE, BY THE WAY.

920
00:43:00,378 --> 00:43:01,747
[SUAVELY]
OW, MY ANKLE.

921
00:43:01,780 --> 00:43:04,850
THANK YOU.

922
00:43:04,883 --> 00:43:06,018
WHAT DO YOU THINK OF IT?

923
00:43:06,052 --> 00:43:07,118
I'D LIKE TO SLEEP
WITH THAT PAINTING.

924
00:43:07,152 --> 00:43:08,520
[KNOCK AT DOOR]
WHAT DO I SAY?

925
00:43:08,553 --> 00:43:10,255
WHOEVER'S KNOCKING
AT YOUR DOOR

926
00:43:10,288 --> 00:43:11,757
IS SOMEONE WHO WANTS
TO SPEAK WITH ME.

927
00:43:11,790 --> 00:43:13,525
BUT I DON'T WANT TO SEE 'EM.

928
00:43:13,558 --> 00:43:14,660
IS THERE ANY PLACE I CAN HIDE?

929
00:43:14,693 --> 00:43:16,195
IN YOUR CLEAVAGE, PERHAPS?

930
00:43:16,228 --> 00:43:19,130
[MAN]
OPEN UP. OPEN UP!

931
00:43:19,163 --> 00:43:20,298
"LATTICE" IN.

932
00:43:20,332 --> 00:43:23,668
[LAUGHTER]
THAT'S A GOOD ONE.

933
00:43:23,702 --> 00:43:27,940
WHAT IN HEAVEN'S NAME
IS GOING ON?

934
00:43:27,973 --> 00:43:30,942
HEY, SHE PAINTS AS GOOD
AS LINDA McCARTNEY?

935
00:43:30,975 --> 00:43:33,045
WELL, WHY ARE YOU
STANDING OUT THERE?

936
00:43:33,078 --> 00:43:35,913
- BOING.
- COME ON IN.

937
00:43:35,947 --> 00:43:38,483
HEH. YOU SEE, WE'RE HERE
ON A BREAST INSPECTION.

938
00:43:38,517 --> 00:43:40,785
YES, YES.

939
00:43:40,818 --> 00:43:42,287
WE'RE LOOKING FOR A MAN.

940
00:43:42,320 --> 00:43:44,255
ARE YOU HIM?

941
00:43:44,288 --> 00:43:46,425
MY WORD.
SO AM I.

942
00:43:46,458 --> 00:43:48,827
LET ME KNOW IF YOU FIND
AN EXTRA ONE.

943
00:43:48,860 --> 00:43:50,928
I THINK YOU KNOW
WHAT I MEANT.

944
00:43:50,962 --> 00:43:53,865
BE SURE AND SHUT THE DOOR.
THERE'S A DRAFT.

945
00:43:53,898 --> 00:43:55,333
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.

946
00:43:55,367 --> 00:43:57,602
'CAUSE I'M NUDE, YOU KNOW.

947
00:43:57,635 --> 00:43:59,103
YOU KNOW,
I'D DROP INTO AN APARTMENT

948
00:43:59,137 --> 00:44:00,738
AND IT WOULD BE BELLA ABZUG.

949
00:44:00,772 --> 00:44:03,242
- WHOA.
- UGH.

950
00:44:03,275 --> 00:44:05,377
YOU CAN COME OUT NOW.
HE'S GONE.

951
00:44:05,410 --> 00:44:07,045
HOW CLEVER, TO THINK
OF HIDING IN THE CLOSET.

952
00:44:07,078 --> 00:44:08,380
WELL, HOW ABOUT THAT, HMM?

953
00:44:08,413 --> 00:44:10,782
- YOU WERE WONDERFUL.
- I TRIED ON YOUR BLUE OUTFIT.

954
00:44:10,815 --> 00:44:13,052
- WHAT I NEED NOW...
- YES?

955
00:44:13,085 --> 00:44:14,285
IS A KING-SIZED CIGARETTE.

956
00:44:14,318 --> 00:44:15,320
SURE. WHY NOT?

957
00:44:15,353 --> 00:44:16,422
- WOW.
- HMM.

958
00:44:16,455 --> 00:44:17,688
I DON'T KNOW WHO YOU ARE,
HONEY,

959
00:44:17,722 --> 00:44:19,257
BUT BART FARGO
OWES YOU A FAVOR.

960
00:44:19,290 --> 00:44:20,425
[LAUGHTER]
BART FARGO.

961
00:44:20,458 --> 00:44:22,260
OH, IN THAT CASE,
TAKE ME OUT TO DINNER.

962
00:44:22,293 --> 00:44:24,397
I HAVEN'T HAD
A SQUARE MEAL IN DAYS?

963
00:44:24,430 --> 00:44:26,298
WHAT'S THE MATTER?
NO MONEY?

964
00:44:26,332 --> 00:44:29,435
MM. NO, I JUST FORGET ALL ABOUT
MEALS WHEN I'M PAINTING.

965
00:44:29,468 --> 00:44:31,070
OH, THAT NAUSEATING, HUH?

966
00:44:31,103 --> 00:44:32,103
LET'S GO TO MY HOTEL.

967
00:44:32,137 --> 00:44:33,738
- WHAT?
- AH, I COULDN'T.

968
00:44:33,772 --> 00:44:36,308
I HAVE A VERY JEALOUS
BOYFRIEND, BART.

969
00:44:36,342 --> 00:44:38,243
WHAT'S THE NAME?

970
00:44:38,277 --> 00:44:39,812
MARK ANTHONY.

971
00:44:39,845 --> 00:44:41,280
NO, I MEANT YOUR NAME.

972
00:44:41,313 --> 00:44:42,848
BRUTUS.

973
00:44:42,882 --> 00:44:43,882
LUCILLE.

974
00:44:43,915 --> 00:44:45,950
[IMITATING LITTLE RICHARD]
LUCILLE!

975
00:44:45,983 --> 00:44:50,422
WELL, LUCILLE, MARK ANTHONY'S
A VERY LUCKY FELLOW.

976
00:44:50,455 --> 00:44:52,157
IT'S BEEN A PLEASURE.

977
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:53,625
I SURE HATE HAVING
TO SEND YOU AWAY,

978
00:44:53,658 --> 00:44:56,228
BUT I'VE GOT
TO FINISH THE PICTURE.

979
00:44:56,262 --> 00:44:58,863
THANKS AGAIN. LUCILLE.

980
00:44:58,897 --> 00:45:02,333
HEY, WHAT'S WITH THE SECRET
AGENT WHO KEEPS STRIKING OUT?

981
00:45:02,367 --> 00:45:05,403
THEY'RE JUST WAITING
OUTSIDE THE DOOR.

982
00:45:09,107 --> 00:45:12,077
WELL, YOU CAN TELL
BY THE WAY I USE MY WALK,

983
00:45:12,110 --> 00:45:15,413
I'M A WOMAN'S MAN,
NO TIME TO TALK.

984
00:45:17,748 --> 00:45:18,750
[KNOCKS]

985
00:45:18,783 --> 00:45:19,785
COME IN.

986
00:45:19,818 --> 00:45:23,622
"LET'S GO TO MY HOTEL."

987
00:45:23,655 --> 00:45:27,793
YOUR BREAKFAST, SENOR.

988
00:45:27,827 --> 00:45:28,860
PUT IT ON THE TABLE.

989
00:45:28,893 --> 00:45:30,962
THEN PUT YOU ON THE ME.

990
00:45:30,995 --> 00:45:34,600
OH, WE ORDERED ONE OF THOSE
CRAPPY EUROPEAN BREAKFASTS.

991
00:45:38,303 --> 00:45:42,273
FRESHLY BAKED.
[CHUCKLES]

992
00:45:42,307 --> 00:45:47,045
SENOR, WE'VE CLEANED
AND PRESSED YOUR GUN.

993
00:45:47,078 --> 00:45:50,448
WE'RE GONNA PUT AN END
TO THIS TOWEL STEALING

994
00:45:50,482 --> 00:45:53,818
ONCE AND FOR ALL!

995
00:45:53,852 --> 00:45:58,123
DAVID CASSIDY IS ABE LINCOLN
BEHIND CONFEDERATE LINES.

996
00:46:00,392 --> 00:46:03,228
OH!

997
00:46:03,262 --> 00:46:07,565
THIS HAPPENED WHEN I WAS
MANNIX'S BELLBOY TOO. OH.

998
00:46:07,598 --> 00:46:10,868
LINCOLN ACTUALLY FOUGHT
GOLDEN GLOVES.

999
00:46:10,902 --> 00:46:11,903
OOH.

1000
00:46:11,937 --> 00:46:13,072
[GROANS]

1001
00:46:13,105 --> 00:46:16,608
OH, I'VE GOT
A RAIL-SPLITTING HEADACHE.

1002
00:46:16,642 --> 00:46:20,578
YOU'RE NO RAYMOND MASSEY
TO US, MR.

1003
00:46:20,612 --> 00:46:22,480
NO, IT'S REAL!

1004
00:46:22,513 --> 00:46:26,418
OH, IT'S...

1005
00:46:26,452 --> 00:46:27,452
YOU KNOW, SCARFACE,

1006
00:46:27,485 --> 00:46:28,953
THAT WAS A VERY SILLY GETUP.

1007
00:46:28,987 --> 00:46:30,988
IT DIDN'T SUIT YOU.

1008
00:46:31,022 --> 00:46:35,293
AND YOUR IMITATION OF A WAITER
WAS VERY FUNNY.

1009
00:46:35,327 --> 00:46:38,797
"YOUR BREAKFAST, SENOR."

1010
00:46:38,830 --> 00:46:42,167
YOU SHOULD HAVE CHANGED
YOUR VOICE TOO.

1011
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:43,802
- OLE.
- AAH!

1012
00:46:43,835 --> 00:46:45,537
AND THE WAY YOU
DOVE OUT THE WINDOW

1013
00:46:45,570 --> 00:46:47,838
WAS JUST TERRIBLE.

1014
00:46:47,872 --> 00:46:49,775
OOH. SORRY, MA'AM.

1015
00:46:49,808 --> 00:46:51,243
THAT'S TOO BAD.

1016
00:46:51,277 --> 00:46:52,310
OH, COME ON!

1017
00:46:52,343 --> 00:46:53,745
WHAT ABOUT
"HE REALLY FELL FOR ME"?

1018
00:46:53,778 --> 00:46:55,013
"HIS HOPES ARE CRUSHED"?

1019
00:46:55,047 --> 00:46:57,015
AH.

1020
00:46:57,048 --> 00:46:58,883
[SIRENS WAILING]

1021
00:47:04,322 --> 00:47:06,258
♪ BARCELONA WANTS ME ♪

1022
00:47:06,292 --> 00:47:10,662
♪ SEE I CAN'T GO BACK THERE ♪

1023
00:47:10,695 --> 00:47:12,898
HEY, YOU MUST HAVE
JUST HAD EYE DROPS.

1024
00:47:12,932 --> 00:47:15,567
HE'S WEARING THOSE ITALIAN,
WOMANY GLASSES.

1025
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:17,368
WHO'S THAT BEHIND
THOSE AMY GRANTS?

1026
00:47:17,402 --> 00:47:18,370
THEY'RE COOL.

1027
00:47:18,403 --> 00:47:21,540
- YEAH?
- YEAH.

1028
00:47:23,442 --> 00:47:27,445
LONG LINE TO THE BARBER SHOP.

1029
00:47:27,478 --> 00:47:31,550
ALL RIGHT, WE'LL COME BACK
FOR THE REST LATER.

1030
00:47:31,583 --> 00:47:32,985
CAN I HAVE PART OF THAT SKULL?

1031
00:47:33,018 --> 00:47:34,987
YEAH, WHAT ARE YOU GONNA DO
WITH THE EXTRA PIECES?

1032
00:47:35,020 --> 00:47:38,423
THERE'S SOME BRAIN OVER HERE.
YOU WANT THIS BRAIN?

1033
00:47:38,457 --> 00:47:39,658
LET'S GO TO THE VILLA.

1034
00:47:39,692 --> 00:47:43,528
SURE, I'D LOVE TO GO
TO THE VILLA WITH YOU.

1035
00:47:43,562 --> 00:47:48,167
TOO SHY.
I SHOULD JUST INTRODUCE MYSELF.

1036
00:47:48,200 --> 00:47:50,202
OH, I SEE HE DRIVES ONE OF THEM
LITTLE FOREIGN JOBS.

1037
00:47:50,235 --> 00:47:52,537
OH, MY CIRCUS MINI CAR.

1038
00:47:52,570 --> 00:47:55,107
[IMITATES CIRCUS MUSIC]

1039
00:47:57,542 --> 00:48:00,378
SHE'S WEARING AN ARMOIRE
ON HER FINGER.

1040
00:48:03,948 --> 00:48:06,150
DANGER.
BIRTH CONTROL PILLS.

1041
00:48:06,183 --> 00:48:07,585
X-9 CALLING.

1042
00:48:07,618 --> 00:48:08,620
- LISTEN, FRANK.
- "LEESTEN?"

1043
00:48:08,653 --> 00:48:10,322
I JUST SAW THE MAN
WE'RE AFTER

1044
00:48:10,355 --> 00:48:11,690
GET INTO A RED SPORT CAR.

1045
00:48:11,723 --> 00:48:14,325
HE'S FOLLOWING YOU.
YOU KNOW WHAT TO DO.

1046
00:48:14,358 --> 00:48:16,595
YEAH, WE KNOW WHAT TO DO.

1047
00:48:16,628 --> 00:48:18,930
[LAUGHS]
WHAT DO WE DO?

1048
00:48:18,963 --> 00:48:21,232
GOD, YOU'RE UGLY.

1049
00:48:24,202 --> 00:48:27,205
OH. I CAN'T SHAKE HIM.
HE'S TOO GOOD.

1050
00:48:29,273 --> 00:48:32,010
I COULD USE A TOUCH
MORE HEAD ROOM.

1051
00:48:35,080 --> 00:48:37,082
I THINK THEY LOST HIM.

1052
00:48:40,452 --> 00:48:43,288
- DAMN HE'S GOOD!
- WOW.

1053
00:48:45,857 --> 00:48:50,428
SPY MOVIE HISTORICAL MARKER,
TWO MILES.

1054
00:48:50,462 --> 00:48:52,430
GO, SPEED RACER.

1055
00:48:52,463 --> 00:48:57,068
GO, SPEED RACER...
[YAWNS]

1056
00:48:57,102 --> 00:49:00,138
IT'S A HIGH-PERFORMANCE
DODGE DART.

1057
00:49:00,172 --> 00:49:03,042
WELL, YOU KNOW, JUST BECAUSE
YOU'RE HAVING A HIGH-SPEED CHASE

1058
00:49:03,075 --> 00:49:05,243
DOESN'T MEAN YOU CAN'T HAVE
AN ADEQUATE SPACE CUSHION.

1059
00:49:05,277 --> 00:49:08,713
MM-HMM.

1060
00:49:08,747 --> 00:49:11,148
UH, SIR, THERE'S A NIPPLE
ON YOUR FACE.

1061
00:49:11,182 --> 00:49:12,317
UGH.

1062
00:49:12,350 --> 00:49:16,153
THIS HIGHWAY ADOPTED
BY THE BARCELONA JCs.

1063
00:49:16,187 --> 00:49:19,223
THE ROCKFORD FILES:
EUROPEAN VACATION.

1064
00:49:21,125 --> 00:49:23,428
WELL, THIS IS THE BIG
CHASE SCENE, FOLKS,

1065
00:49:23,462 --> 00:49:24,763
SO YOU MIGHT WANNA
TAKE THIS TIME

1066
00:49:24,797 --> 00:49:25,830
TO GO MAKE YOURSELF
A SANDWICH

1067
00:49:25,863 --> 00:49:27,432
OR TAKE A SHOWER OR...

1068
00:49:27,465 --> 00:49:28,900
HE EMPTIED THE URINAL.

1069
00:49:28,933 --> 00:49:31,168
[TIRES SCREECHING]

1070
00:49:31,202 --> 00:49:33,705
OOH.

1071
00:49:33,738 --> 00:49:35,173
HOT WHEELS.

1072
00:49:35,207 --> 00:49:38,810
SOME LITTLE BOY
IS GOING TO BE VERY UPSET.

1073
00:49:42,247 --> 00:49:44,482
AH-HA. I THINK WE JUST
FOILED SOMEONE,

1074
00:49:44,515 --> 00:49:47,552
BUT BECAUSE OF THE EDITING,
I'M NOT REALLY SURE.

1075
00:49:47,585 --> 00:49:50,022
THEY TAMPERED
IN GOD'S DOMAIN.

1076
00:49:54,125 --> 00:49:55,127
LET'S GET MOVING.

1077
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:56,862
OH, WHAT KIND
OF A LAME QUIP IS THAT?

1078
00:49:56,895 --> 00:49:58,363
WHAT ABOUT, "HE'S ALL WET"?

1079
00:49:58,397 --> 00:49:59,732
OR "HE TOOK A DIP"?

1080
00:49:59,765 --> 00:50:01,500
YEAH, OR "HE MADE
QUITE A SPLASH"?

1081
00:50:01,533 --> 00:50:03,535
HMM.

1082
00:50:07,872 --> 00:50:09,007
WHOA-HO!

1083
00:50:09,040 --> 00:50:11,342
PORTRAIT OF THE ARTIST
AS A YOUNG VA-VOOM!

1084
00:50:11,375 --> 00:50:12,543
[KNOCK AT DOOR]

1085
00:50:12,577 --> 00:50:15,147
- THE DOOR'S UNLOCKED.
- AND SO AM I.

1086
00:50:15,180 --> 00:50:16,748
JUST PUSH.

1087
00:50:16,782 --> 00:50:19,383
[SNEEZES]

1088
00:50:19,417 --> 00:50:21,285
HI, LUCILLE.

1089
00:50:21,318 --> 00:50:23,955
WHY, WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

1090
00:50:23,988 --> 00:50:25,123
I WENT FOR A SWIM.

1091
00:50:25,157 --> 00:50:26,958
AH, SEE, AT LEAST
HE TRIED TO QUIT.

1092
00:50:26,992 --> 00:50:28,093
YOU MUST BE CRAZY.

1093
00:50:28,127 --> 00:50:29,227
MAYBE YOU'RE RIGHT.

1094
00:50:29,260 --> 00:50:30,695
I CAN TELL YOU RIGHT NOW

1095
00:50:30,728 --> 00:50:32,430
I'M NOT VERY GOOD
AT PRESSING TROUSERS,

1096
00:50:32,463 --> 00:50:34,565
- BUT I'LL DO MY BEST.
- MM.

1097
00:50:34,598 --> 00:50:35,900
- TAKE EVERYTHING OFF.
- [GASPS]

1098
00:50:35,933 --> 00:50:37,035
YOU'RE NOT SHY, ARE YOU?

1099
00:50:37,068 --> 00:50:39,137
NOT REALLY,
BUT DO YOU HAVE SOMETHING

1100
00:50:39,170 --> 00:50:41,005
A LITTLE BIT DRIER
I CAN SLIP INTO?

1101
00:50:41,038 --> 00:50:43,007
IN CASE YOU DIDN'T KNOW,

1102
00:50:43,040 --> 00:50:45,143
THIS IS THE LIGHT-HEARTED
PORTION OF OUR MOVIE.

1103
00:50:45,177 --> 00:50:46,277
[GOOFY LAUGHTER]

1104
00:50:46,310 --> 00:50:48,880
YOU MEN ARE FULL
OF THE STRANGEST COMPLEXES.

1105
00:50:48,913 --> 00:50:51,215
TO TELL YOU THE TRUTH,
RIGHT NOW

1106
00:50:51,248 --> 00:50:52,983
I'D RATHER
BE FULL OF SCOTCH.

1107
00:50:53,017 --> 00:50:54,787
THERE'S SOME COOKING BRANDY
IN THE KITCHEN.

1108
00:50:54,820 --> 00:50:57,655
DO YOU HAVE HOLLAND HOUSE?

1109
00:50:57,688 --> 00:51:00,858
YOU KNOW, I STILL THINK
MY IDEA'S BEST.

1110
00:51:00,892 --> 00:51:01,893
THAT I WEAR YOUR DRESS.

1111
00:51:01,927 --> 00:51:03,395
AS SOON AS YOU'VE FINISHED,

1112
00:51:03,428 --> 00:51:04,830
WE'LL GO OUT
AND HAVE A DRINK.

1113
00:51:04,863 --> 00:51:07,232
AH, FIRST YOU WANT
TO GET ME HIGH,

1114
00:51:07,265 --> 00:51:08,567
AND THEN
YOU'LL TAKE ADVANTAGE.

1115
00:51:08,600 --> 00:51:09,600
BINGO!

1116
00:51:09,633 --> 00:51:11,503
TWO SIPS, BART,
AND I'M JUST LOST.

1117
00:51:11,537 --> 00:51:12,870
OH, COME ON.

1118
00:51:12,903 --> 00:51:14,072
YOU WOULDN'T REFUSE A MAN

1119
00:51:14,105 --> 00:51:16,073
WHO'S ABOUT TO DIE
OF PNEUMONIA, WOULD YOU?

1120
00:51:16,107 --> 00:51:18,843
I DON'T DATE KEN DOLLS.

1121
00:51:20,678 --> 00:51:22,113
HUH?

1122
00:51:22,147 --> 00:51:24,983
OH, NOW IT'S
AN ERMA BOMBECK COLUMN.

1123
00:51:25,017 --> 00:51:28,118
HEY.
SHE'S A TOILET PAPER COSIE.

1124
00:51:28,152 --> 00:51:30,288
IN A SALUTE TO NAIR.

1125
00:51:35,560 --> 00:51:36,995
YES, YES, HERE WE GO.

1126
00:51:37,028 --> 00:51:41,165
WE'LL PUT YOU IN THE BACK,
BECAUSE OF YOUR OUTFIT AND ALL.

1127
00:51:41,198 --> 00:51:43,268
[LOUDLY] I THOUGHT
THIS WOULD BE A GOOD PLACE

1128
00:51:43,302 --> 00:51:45,837
TO JUST TALK, TO GET
TO KNOW EACH OTHER.

1129
00:51:45,870 --> 00:51:47,438
TWO WHISKEYS ON THE ROCKS.

1130
00:51:47,472 --> 00:51:48,473
YES, SIR.

1131
00:51:48,507 --> 00:51:50,675
DON'T BE STINGY, BABY.

1132
00:51:53,378 --> 00:51:54,345
THIS MAKES THE CHASE SCENE

1133
00:51:54,378 --> 00:51:58,817
LOOK ABSOLUTELY EXHILARATING.

1134
00:51:58,850 --> 00:52:02,820
MISS ICEBERG LETTUCE.

1135
00:52:02,853 --> 00:52:04,322
THAT'S VICTOR/VICTORIA.

1136
00:52:04,355 --> 00:52:06,725
NEXT UP, SANDLER AND YOUNG.

1137
00:52:11,930 --> 00:52:14,398
CAN'T BELIEVE
SHE'S DOING MY BIT.

1138
00:52:14,432 --> 00:52:17,702
AL. AL.

1139
00:52:17,735 --> 00:52:18,970
WHAT IS IT?

1140
00:52:19,003 --> 00:52:20,638
HE'S OUT THERE.
THE AMERICAN.

1141
00:52:20,672 --> 00:52:24,008
YOU BETTER HURRY.
WARN THE BOSS.

1142
00:52:24,042 --> 00:52:28,480
GOT TO GET OUT OF THIS MOVIE.

1143
00:52:28,513 --> 00:52:30,848
NOW, SEE, YOU SHOULD NEVER
WEAR WHITE PANTS ON A CAPER.

1144
00:52:30,882 --> 00:52:32,250
THIS IS WHY.

1145
00:52:32,283 --> 00:52:35,620
JEEZ, I WISH THEY'D
INVENT ELEVATORS.

1146
00:52:35,653 --> 00:52:38,357
THINK HE'S A CLANDESTINE
WINDOW WASHER.

1147
00:52:39,992 --> 00:52:42,993
[IMITATING JAZZ MUSIC]

1148
00:52:47,032 --> 00:52:49,667
[WHISPERING]
HONEY. HONEY, I'M HOME.

1149
00:52:49,700 --> 00:52:52,070
HONEY.

1150
00:52:56,573 --> 00:52:57,675
[LAUGHS]

1151
00:52:57,708 --> 00:53:00,112
IT'S LIKE WALKING
EXCEPT DIFFERENT.

1152
00:53:00,145 --> 00:53:02,147
IT'S LATE.
WE'D BETTER GO.

1153
00:53:02,180 --> 00:53:04,482
UH, DO YOU MIND
IF I DRIVE THIS TIME?

1154
00:53:04,515 --> 00:53:05,583
AW.

1155
00:53:05,617 --> 00:53:08,453
IS THIS THE NATIONAL
TWISTER MONUMENT?

1156
00:53:08,487 --> 00:53:13,090
WHOA.
A JUMPSUIT-LESS BACK.

1157
00:53:13,123 --> 00:53:16,227
ARE YOU A DARING YOUNG MAN
IN A JAUNTY JALOPY?

1158
00:53:25,570 --> 00:53:29,407
AH, WHY DON'T THEY
MAKE IT GO FORWARD?

1159
00:53:29,440 --> 00:53:32,443
WELL,
FINALLY GOT RID OF HER.

1160
00:53:32,477 --> 00:53:34,212
ALL SECRET AGENTS ARE GUESTS

1161
00:53:34,245 --> 00:53:38,317
OF THE LUXURIOUS MOTEL SIX.

1162
00:53:38,350 --> 00:53:40,818
LUCKY GUESS, I GOTTA ADMIT.

1163
00:53:40,852 --> 00:53:42,653
[TELEPHONE RINGS]

1164
00:53:42,687 --> 00:53:47,125
I'LL GET IT.

1165
00:53:47,158 --> 00:53:48,960
WOW.
SWINGING BACHELOR PAD.

1166
00:53:48,993 --> 00:53:51,462
HELLO?
YEAH, I JUST GOT IN.

1167
00:53:51,495 --> 00:53:52,663
YEAH, THE GUY WITH THE KNIFE
IS STILL HERE.

1168
00:53:52,697 --> 00:53:55,033
THANKS FOR A SWELL EVENING.

1169
00:53:55,067 --> 00:53:58,770
[LAUGHS]
OKAY.

1170
00:53:58,803 --> 00:54:01,138
NO JUMPING ON THE BED.

1171
00:54:03,708 --> 00:54:05,610
- WHOA.
- HEY, NO, DON'T.

1172
00:54:05,643 --> 00:54:06,778
- STOP IT.
- OH.

1173
00:54:06,812 --> 00:54:09,180
BART. BART!

1174
00:54:09,213 --> 00:54:11,548
WHAT'S GOING ON, DARLING?

1175
00:54:11,582 --> 00:54:15,353
DADDY IS ON THE PHONE!

1176
00:54:15,387 --> 00:54:16,822
MY MOTHER, MY SISTER,

1177
00:54:16,855 --> 00:54:18,255
MY SISTER, MY MOTHER!

1178
00:54:18,288 --> 00:54:21,660
HIS NAME IS LUCA.

1179
00:54:21,693 --> 00:54:24,262
I'M SENDING YOU TO BED
WITHOUT ROOM SERVICE.

1180
00:54:27,132 --> 00:54:30,468
WELL, I'M GONNA ORDER.
YOU WANT ANYTHING.

1181
00:54:30,502 --> 00:54:32,203
SORRY FOR THAT, DARLING.
IT WAS ROOM SERVICE.

1182
00:54:32,237 --> 00:54:33,203
I'M KIDDING.

1183
00:54:33,237 --> 00:54:34,205
WHAT DID YOU WANT
TO TELL ME?

1184
00:54:34,238 --> 00:54:36,273
THAT I'M MAD ABOUT YOU.

1185
00:54:36,307 --> 00:54:37,775
- OOH.
- YOU SAY IT LIKE YOU MEAN IT.

1186
00:54:37,808 --> 00:54:40,012
OF COURSE I DO, BART.

1187
00:54:40,045 --> 00:54:41,012
I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

1188
00:54:41,045 --> 00:54:42,047
MWAH. MWAH.

1189
00:54:42,080 --> 00:54:44,015
SURE. BYE.

1190
00:54:47,685 --> 00:54:50,555
GUN PLACED BY THE GIDEON'S.

1191
00:54:54,225 --> 00:54:56,928
YOU AND I HAVE SOME ISSUES,
MISTER.

1192
00:54:56,962 --> 00:54:58,363
ALL RIGHT, TALK.

1193
00:54:58,397 --> 00:55:00,365
WHERE'S PROFESSOR CARMICHAEL?

1194
00:55:00,398 --> 00:55:02,067
COULD YOU SLAP ME AGAIN?

1195
00:55:02,100 --> 00:55:05,603
IF I TELL YOU, THE BOSS'LL
HAVE ME KILLED.

1196
00:55:05,637 --> 00:55:07,205
SPRINGSTEEN? WHY?

1197
00:55:07,238 --> 00:55:08,873
PLEASE TRY TO UNDERSTAND.

1198
00:55:08,907 --> 00:55:10,342
I'M GARY CROSBY.

1199
00:55:10,375 --> 00:55:12,510
LISTEN, YOU TELL ME, OR YOU'RE
GONNA BE IN REAL TROUBLE.

1200
00:55:12,543 --> 00:55:16,915
I'LL SPANK YOU, I WILL.

1201
00:55:16,948 --> 00:55:20,952
YOU JUST WAIT
TILL YOUR FATHER GETS HOME.

1202
00:55:20,985 --> 00:55:22,787
[WITH ACCENT]
HOUSEKEEPING.

1203
00:55:22,820 --> 00:55:25,757
HELLO?

1204
00:55:25,790 --> 00:55:28,092
OH, I DON'T NEED
ANYMORE TOILET PAPER.

1205
00:55:28,125 --> 00:55:29,127
OH, PARDON.

1206
00:55:29,160 --> 00:55:30,395
I THOUGHT IT WAS MY ROOM.

1207
00:55:30,428 --> 00:55:32,763
WHY, IT'S YOU.
WHAT A COINCIDENCE.

1208
00:55:32,797 --> 00:55:37,068
JUST LOVE THE VIEW
FROM THIS ROOM.

1209
00:55:37,102 --> 00:55:39,603
- COME BACK HERE.
- YOU HAVE BOTH ROOM KEYS.

1210
00:55:39,637 --> 00:55:42,940
- HEY.
- YOU OWE ME FOR PART
OF THE BILL.

1211
00:55:47,445 --> 00:55:48,413
AH.

1212
00:55:48,447 --> 00:55:49,847
HE'S GOT SUCH A SOFT SPOT

1213
00:55:49,880 --> 00:55:52,417
FOR PEOPLE
WHO TRY TO KILL HIM.

1214
00:55:52,450 --> 00:55:55,120
YOU SEE, A LONG TIME AGO,
I LOST A BALL UP HERE--

1215
00:55:55,153 --> 00:55:57,822
OH, THERE IT IS.

1216
00:56:02,027 --> 00:56:03,762
WELL, THAT MOMENT
WENT NOWHERE.

1217
00:56:03,795 --> 00:56:05,197
I'M GONNA GO BACK IN.

1218
00:56:05,230 --> 00:56:06,630
I'M HERE TO REGISTER VOTERS.

1219
00:56:06,663 --> 00:56:08,667
I HOPE I DIDN'T
INTERRUPT ANYTHING.

1220
00:56:08,700 --> 00:56:09,700
ANYTHING WRONG?

1221
00:56:09,733 --> 00:56:10,835
JUST A BURGLAR.

1222
00:56:10,868 --> 00:56:12,970
I'M SORRY.
IT'S ALL MY FAULT.

1223
00:56:13,003 --> 00:56:15,072
YOU SEE,
MY ROOM'S NEXT DOOR.

1224
00:56:15,105 --> 00:56:17,942
THE HALL'S SO BADLY LIT,
I COULDN'T READ THE NUMBER.

1225
00:56:17,975 --> 00:56:20,412
I REALLY AM SORRY.
I WAS SO SILLY.

1226
00:56:20,445 --> 00:56:22,813
DON'T WORRY.
WHY DON'T YOU COME IN
FOR A MINUTE?

1227
00:56:22,847 --> 00:56:26,250
WELL, NOW THAT FATE'S
BROUGHT US TOGETHER AGAIN

1228
00:56:26,283 --> 00:56:27,718
WE CAN GET TO KNOW
EACH OTHER BETTER.

1229
00:56:27,752 --> 00:56:29,987
I LIKE BOBBY VINTON.

1230
00:56:30,020 --> 00:56:31,155
WHOA.

1231
00:56:31,188 --> 00:56:33,525
BART, LET'S GO FOR A RIDE
IN A MOTORBOAT.

1232
00:56:33,558 --> 00:56:34,958
IT'S WONDERFUL
IN THE FIRST LIGHT.

1233
00:56:34,992 --> 00:56:37,128
WELL, WHAT DO YOU SAY?

1234
00:56:37,162 --> 00:56:41,332
OKAY! VROOM, VROOM.
[LAUGHS]

1235
00:56:41,365 --> 00:56:43,835
I FEEL LIKE KISSING
HIS SHOULDER. IS THAT WEIRD?

1236
00:56:43,868 --> 00:56:44,868
UM...

1237
00:56:44,902 --> 00:56:47,705
OH.

1238
00:56:47,738 --> 00:56:50,675
I'LL NEED MY PURSE
FOR THE SHOWER.

1239
00:56:55,447 --> 00:56:57,382
YOU HAVEN'T SAID ANYTHING
ABOUT YOUR WORK.

1240
00:56:57,415 --> 00:57:00,552
I SHOULD THINK THAT
BARCELONA'S A GOOD CENTER.

1241
00:57:00,585 --> 00:57:02,287
FOR YOUR LINE OF BUSINESS.

1242
00:57:02,320 --> 00:57:04,588
OH, UH, DON'T LOOK
ON THE TOP SHELF IN THERE,

1243
00:57:04,622 --> 00:57:06,290
'CAUSE--GUY
WHO LIVED HERE BEFORE

1244
00:57:06,323 --> 00:57:07,525
HAD A LOT OF PORNO MAGAZINES.

1245
00:57:07,558 --> 00:57:11,728
...QUITE A DEMAND
FOR OUR PRODUCTS IN SPAIN.

1246
00:57:11,762 --> 00:57:15,132
- WELL, HELLO.
- THIS IS FOR THE LADIES.

1247
00:57:15,165 --> 00:57:18,970
BUT I LIKE IT TOO.

1248
00:57:19,003 --> 00:57:21,705
IF YOU WANT TO GO TO THE POLICE
ABOUT THAT BURGLAR,

1249
00:57:21,738 --> 00:57:24,442
I CAN TAKE YOU THERE AFTER
OUR TRIP IN THE MOTORBOAT.

1250
00:57:24,475 --> 00:57:27,312
YOU SEE, THE CHIEF OF POLICE,
HE'S AN OLD FRIEND OF MINE.

1251
00:57:27,345 --> 00:57:29,513
IT ALWAYS HELPS
TO KNOW SOMEONE.

1252
00:57:29,547 --> 00:57:31,115
THANKS.
I MAY AS WELL,

1253
00:57:31,148 --> 00:57:33,852
BUT I DON'T THINK
IT'LL BE EASY TO CATCH HIM.

1254
00:57:33,885 --> 00:57:36,720
I REALLY ENJOY
OUR MUNDANE CONVERSATION.

1255
00:57:38,890 --> 00:57:41,425
THE BOATNIKS: UNDERCOVER.

1256
00:57:41,458 --> 00:57:45,497
THAT'S WAY TOO FAST TO TROLL.

1257
00:57:45,530 --> 00:57:49,367
I AM DETERMINED TO GET
A MUSKY THIS YEAR.

1258
00:57:53,370 --> 00:57:56,007
THIS MAN, OOH...

1259
00:57:58,408 --> 00:57:59,810
IT WAS AN INTERESTING CHOICE

1260
00:57:59,843 --> 00:58:02,047
NOT TO HAVE ANY SUSPENSE
IN THIS MOVIE.

1261
00:58:02,080 --> 00:58:03,080
I KNOW.

1262
00:58:03,113 --> 00:58:04,682
THIS IS THE LOW-BUDGET REMAKE

1263
00:58:04,715 --> 00:58:06,650
OF A NIGHT TO REMEMBER.

1264
00:58:06,683 --> 00:58:08,653
WHY DON'T WE DO
A BIT OF SUNBATHING?

1265
00:58:08,687 --> 00:58:09,687
SURE.

1266
00:58:09,720 --> 00:58:13,257
TEACH ME.

1267
00:58:13,290 --> 00:58:15,092
AH.

1268
00:58:15,125 --> 00:58:17,162
WHOA.

1269
00:58:17,195 --> 00:58:20,365
OOH.

1270
00:58:20,398 --> 00:58:21,900
- WOULD YOU LIKE A CIGARETTE?
- PLEASE.

1271
00:58:21,933 --> 00:58:23,668
- THEY'RE DONE ALREADY?
- WOW.

1272
00:58:23,702 --> 00:58:26,837
HE'S NOT ITALIAN.

1273
00:58:26,870 --> 00:58:28,305
THERE'S A LITTLE BOMB IN IT,

1274
00:58:28,338 --> 00:58:30,308
SO DON'T BE ALARMED
WHEN IT GOES OFF.

1275
00:58:30,342 --> 00:58:32,910
HEY,
THAT'S PREMATURE FOREPLAY.

1276
00:58:35,178 --> 00:58:36,347
DARLING CAPEZIOS.

1277
00:58:36,380 --> 00:58:38,817
MM-HMM.

1278
00:58:38,850 --> 00:58:43,220
THEY'RE HAVING SOME
MONTCLAIR MOMENTS.

1279
00:58:43,253 --> 00:58:47,725
♪ WATERMELON MAN ♪

1280
00:58:47,758 --> 00:58:51,662
GOD, I WAS GREAT.

1281
00:58:51,695 --> 00:58:52,797
AHH.

1282
00:58:52,830 --> 00:58:54,932
SHE'S CHECKING
THE SUN'S MAKEUP.

1283
00:58:54,965 --> 00:58:57,268
OBEY.

1284
00:59:00,137 --> 00:59:04,208
- WHOA.
- HUH?

1285
00:59:04,242 --> 00:59:05,208
OH, HE'S WEARING PULL-UPS.

1286
00:59:05,242 --> 00:59:07,078
OH.

1287
00:59:07,112 --> 00:59:08,412
LET'S GO.

1288
00:59:12,583 --> 00:59:17,055
WHERE'S LIEUTENANT
STEPHANIE HOLDEN
WHEN YOU NEED HER?

1289
00:59:17,088 --> 00:59:19,523
THEY MUST HAVE HIT AN EELPOUT.

1290
00:59:19,557 --> 00:59:22,260
REALLY GO UP.

1291
00:59:29,100 --> 00:59:33,337
HE REALLY NEEDS A TERRY TOP
TO GO WITH THOSE SWIM TRUNKS.

1292
00:59:33,370 --> 00:59:37,808
[SCATTING TO JAZZ MUSIC]

1293
00:59:37,842 --> 00:59:42,447
DEVIL IS THAT SWINGLE SINGER
MUSIC COMING FROM?

1294
00:59:42,480 --> 00:59:44,548
GIVE ME SOME PANTS!

1295
00:59:49,353 --> 00:59:50,355
POW.

1296
00:59:50,388 --> 00:59:53,858
- AAH!
- AAH! SORRY, MS. RENO.

1297
00:59:55,192 --> 00:59:57,328
HA. SHE'S NOT YOUNG
AND BEAUTIFUL, YOU SEE.

1298
01:00:02,200 --> 01:00:04,502
WARDROBE.
MORE PANTS, PLEASE.

1299
01:00:04,535 --> 01:00:08,372
NOW.

1300
01:00:08,405 --> 01:00:11,508
OH...

1301
01:00:11,542 --> 01:00:14,145
UGH. WELL, IT'S 10:00 A.M.
SOMEWHERE IN THE WORLD.

1302
01:00:17,082 --> 01:00:20,385
OH, NO.
I'LL NEVER LOVE AGAIN.

1303
01:00:21,718 --> 01:00:24,822
JERRY REED IS POLONIUS.

1304
01:00:32,163 --> 01:00:34,065
MOIST.

1305
01:00:34,098 --> 01:00:35,833
THAT ROBE HAS
"FATHER'S DAY GIFT"

1306
01:00:35,867 --> 01:00:36,867
WRITTEN ALL OVER IT.

1307
01:00:36,900 --> 01:00:37,902
OOH.

1308
01:00:37,935 --> 01:00:40,270
NEEDS A BAND-AID.

1309
01:00:40,303 --> 01:00:41,972
AAH!

1310
01:00:45,677 --> 01:00:48,747
JERRY REED IN
WHOSE LIFE IS IT ANYWAY?

1311
01:00:50,882 --> 01:00:52,117
LITTLE MURPHY'S OIL SOAP.

1312
01:00:52,150 --> 01:00:53,785
- [GROANS]
- OH.

1313
01:00:53,818 --> 01:00:56,753
[IMITATING CHEMICAL
BURNING SKIN]

1314
01:00:56,787 --> 01:00:58,622
HAVE A SWALLOW.
HERE.

1315
01:00:58,655 --> 01:01:02,993
IT'S TWO FOR ONE.
[CHUCKLES]

1316
01:01:03,027 --> 01:01:05,262
THANKS.

1317
01:01:05,295 --> 01:01:06,930
WELL THEN, DO YOU WANT
TO TALK ABOUT IT?

1318
01:01:06,963 --> 01:01:08,598
HOW DID IT HAPPEN?

1319
01:01:08,632 --> 01:01:10,635
THEY WANTED TO GET RID OF ME.

1320
01:01:10,668 --> 01:01:12,970
- BECAUSE...
- I'M JERRY REED.

1321
01:01:13,003 --> 01:01:14,972
I'M NO USE TO THEM ANYMORE.

1322
01:01:15,005 --> 01:01:17,275
AND SO YOU MANAGED
TO GET AWAY.

1323
01:01:17,308 --> 01:01:19,143
ANOTHER TIME.

1324
01:01:19,177 --> 01:01:21,078
I'VE GOT YOU TO THANK.

1325
01:01:21,112 --> 01:01:24,015
LAST NIGHT OUT THERE YOU HAD
A PERFECT CHANCE TO KILL ME.

1326
01:01:24,048 --> 01:01:25,983
BUT LUCKILY FOR ME,
YOU DIDN'T.

1327
01:01:26,017 --> 01:01:27,318
YOU WANNA
HAVE COFFEE SOMETIME?

1328
01:01:27,352 --> 01:01:30,187
YOU SAVED ME.
SURE IS A BIG DEBT TO REPAY.

1329
01:01:30,220 --> 01:01:32,055
AH, FORGET IT.

1330
01:01:32,088 --> 01:01:34,258
OUR HAIR IS OUR SPECIAL BOND.

1331
01:01:34,292 --> 01:01:36,127
HOW ABOUT ANSWERING
THAT QUESTION.

1332
01:01:36,160 --> 01:01:38,830
YES. I WILL BE
MRS. BART FARGO.

1333
01:01:38,863 --> 01:01:42,500
[TELEPHONE RINGING]

1334
01:01:42,533 --> 01:01:45,670
WHAT IS THAT SOUND?

1335
01:01:45,703 --> 01:01:48,372
YOU'RE OFFICIAL
UCLA BRUINS ROBE.

1336
01:01:48,405 --> 01:01:50,340
HELLO?

1337
01:01:50,373 --> 01:01:52,143
I WAS WAITING FOR YOU, BART.

1338
01:01:52,177 --> 01:01:54,478
- HEY, LISTEN.
- HELLO?

1339
01:01:54,512 --> 01:01:57,115
ABOUT 13 MILES AWAY
ON THE NORTH ROAD OUT OF TOWN,

1340
01:01:57,148 --> 01:02:00,050
THERE'S A VILLA.
GO THERE TONIGHT.

1341
01:02:00,083 --> 01:02:03,320
- YOU BETTER BE CAREFUL.
- HEY, WAIT.

1342
01:02:03,353 --> 01:02:05,923
SHE'S PAINTED
FOR A LAUGH-IN SKETCH.

1343
01:02:05,957 --> 01:02:07,192
BART, WHAT'S GOING ON?

1344
01:02:07,225 --> 01:02:09,160
HOW WOULD I KNOW?
WHAT AM I? A SPY OR SOMETHING?

1345
01:02:09,193 --> 01:02:12,095
SORRY, LUCILLE.
IT WAS THE PORTER.

1346
01:02:12,128 --> 01:02:14,832
HE WAS BRINGING MY LAUNDRY.

1347
01:02:14,865 --> 01:02:16,700
THERE'S ALWAYS SOMEONE THERE
WHEN I CALL.

1348
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:19,003
LISTEN,
HOW ABOUT COMING OVER HERE?

1349
01:02:19,037 --> 01:02:20,772
WE CAN HAVE A QUIET,
LITTLE TALK.

1350
01:02:20,805 --> 01:02:22,140
BUT YOU'RE A GIRL.

1351
01:02:22,173 --> 01:02:23,773
SORRY, I'M VERY BUSY TODAY.

1352
01:02:23,807 --> 01:02:26,110
YOU'RE NOT GIVING ME
THE BRUSH-UP, ARE YOU?

1353
01:02:26,143 --> 01:02:28,245
CERTAINLY NOT,
AND YOU SHOULD KNOW.

1354
01:02:28,278 --> 01:02:30,447
IN THAT CASE,
WHAT ARE YOU WAITING FOR?

1355
01:02:30,480 --> 01:02:33,183
OH, BART,
I DIDN'T SLEEP ALL NIGHT.

1356
01:02:33,217 --> 01:02:34,952
WELL, THEN SHE SHOULD
JUST GET SOME SLEEP.

1357
01:02:34,985 --> 01:02:36,187
NEITHER DID I.

1358
01:02:36,220 --> 01:02:39,223
I REALLY THINK
I'M IN LOVE WITH YOU, BART.

1359
01:02:39,257 --> 01:02:42,927
WITH MARC ANTHONY, IT WAS
A DIFFERENT THING ALTOGETHER.

1360
01:02:42,960 --> 01:02:44,528
YOU KNOW, AN INFATUATION.

1361
01:02:44,562 --> 01:02:45,630
WITH YOU IT'S AN OBSESSION.

1362
01:02:45,663 --> 01:02:46,663
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT.

1363
01:02:46,697 --> 01:02:48,232
I'LL PICK YOU UP
TOMORROW AFTERNOON

1364
01:02:48,265 --> 01:02:49,600
AND WE'LL GO OUT
IN THE BOAT, OKAY?

1365
01:02:49,633 --> 01:02:51,668
YES, DARLING.
BUT COME AS SOON AS YOU CAN.

1366
01:02:51,702 --> 01:02:52,703
SURE.

1367
01:02:52,737 --> 01:02:54,172
THAT'S WHAT I USUALLY DO.

1368
01:02:57,708 --> 01:02:59,010
YOU IDIOT.

1369
01:02:59,043 --> 01:03:00,945
I TOLD YOU TO GET RID OF AL.

1370
01:03:00,978 --> 01:03:03,213
BUT AT LEAST I WOUNDED HIM.

1371
01:03:03,247 --> 01:03:05,448
HE COULDN'T BE VERY FAR.

1372
01:03:05,482 --> 01:03:06,983
AND IF HE'S GOT AWAY?

1373
01:03:07,017 --> 01:03:08,385
IT'S A LIQUOR SHOWROOM.

1374
01:03:08,418 --> 01:03:10,888
DON'T WORRY, SENOR FRANK.
IT'S ALL RIGHT.

1375
01:03:10,922 --> 01:03:12,223
I'LL TAKE CARE OF HIM.

1376
01:03:12,257 --> 01:03:14,125
IF THAT AMERICAN AGENT
GETS A HOLD OF HIM,

1377
01:03:14,158 --> 01:03:15,560
HE'LL FIND OUT
WHERE THE FILL IS.

1378
01:03:15,593 --> 01:03:17,295
I'LL FIND OUT,
SENOR FRANK.

1379
01:03:17,328 --> 01:03:18,930
I'LL KILL HIM
WITH MY OWN HANDS.

1380
01:03:18,963 --> 01:03:23,567
HEY,
LEAVE MR. FRENCH ALONE!

1381
01:03:23,600 --> 01:03:24,802
JEEZ, COPPOLA'S LITTLE.

1382
01:03:24,835 --> 01:03:27,938
SI, SENOR. AT ONCE.

1383
01:03:30,207 --> 01:03:31,208
TACO.

1384
01:03:31,242 --> 01:03:34,612
♪ PUTTIN' ON THE RITZ ♪

1385
01:03:34,645 --> 01:03:36,413
I'M A LITTLE LATE.

1386
01:03:36,447 --> 01:03:37,482
BUT, SENOR...

1387
01:03:37,515 --> 01:03:39,750
THAT'S ALL
I CAN THINK TO SAY.

1388
01:03:39,783 --> 01:03:42,620
HE JUST HAD
HIS SUIT POLISHED.

1389
01:03:46,623 --> 01:03:47,958
OKAY, HI, EVERYBODY.
I'M HERE.

1390
01:03:47,992 --> 01:03:50,093
THE PARTY CAN START.
HELLO.

1391
01:03:52,397 --> 01:03:54,298
HAVE YOU HEARD
ABOUT THE GUY WHO'S LATE?

1392
01:03:54,332 --> 01:03:55,600
THERE'S A LATE GUY HERE.

1393
01:03:55,633 --> 01:04:00,003
THAT'S HIM OVER THERE.
I HEAR HE'S LATE.

1394
01:04:00,037 --> 01:04:01,372
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,

1395
01:04:01,405 --> 01:04:05,408
THE PIZZA ROLLS
WILL BE READY AT ANY MOMENT.

1396
01:04:05,442 --> 01:04:08,178
THE VIPER ROOM'S
KIND OF A LETDOWN.

1397
01:04:08,212 --> 01:04:12,883
APPARENTLY SHINY SUITS
HAVEN'T CAUGHT ON OVER HERE.

1398
01:04:12,917 --> 01:04:15,318
HE ADJUSTED HIS HEAD.

1399
01:04:15,352 --> 01:04:19,590
PAGING MR. FART BAR--
BART FARGO.

1400
01:04:19,623 --> 01:04:21,992
BART FARGO.

1401
01:04:25,128 --> 01:04:28,765
B-49. B-49.

1402
01:04:28,798 --> 01:04:30,568
WHY'D THEY SEAT HIM
AT THE POOL TABLE?

1403
01:04:37,007 --> 01:04:38,108
MADAMS AND MONSIEURS,

1404
01:04:38,142 --> 01:04:39,910
THE BANK, $10,000.

1405
01:04:39,943 --> 01:04:43,347
BETTER BE A DAMN GOOD BONK.

1406
01:04:43,380 --> 01:04:44,648
I'LL CALL.

1407
01:04:44,682 --> 01:04:47,250
GOD, HE'S BEAUTIFUL.

1408
01:04:47,283 --> 01:04:48,752
HE DIDN'T SHOW A CARD
OR ANYTHING.

1409
01:04:48,785 --> 01:04:50,220
THERE, THE MAN
WITH HIS BACK TURNED.

1410
01:04:50,253 --> 01:04:54,158
IT'S PRINCE SAMMY CAHN.

1411
01:04:54,192 --> 01:04:55,693
WHO ARE YOU, PLEASE?

1412
01:04:55,727 --> 01:04:58,228
IF IT'S ANY BUSINESS OF YOURS,
MY GOOD MAN,

1413
01:04:58,262 --> 01:05:01,865
I'M A GUEST.

1414
01:05:01,898 --> 01:05:05,202
[IMITATING TRUMAN CAPOTE]
THAT'S NOT WRITING,
THAT'S TYPING.

1415
01:05:05,235 --> 01:05:06,570
SEVEN FOR MONSIEUR LAUER.

1416
01:05:06,603 --> 01:05:08,238
PALMOLIVE HANDS.

1417
01:05:08,272 --> 01:05:12,208
HMM.

1418
01:05:12,242 --> 01:05:15,212
AND EIGHT
FOR MONSIEUR CHARLTON.

1419
01:05:15,245 --> 01:05:18,148
MR. CHARLTON, IT'S AMAZING THAT
YOU HAVE SUCH A BEAUTIFUL WIFE,

1420
01:05:18,182 --> 01:05:20,083
AND YET YOU STILL MANAGE
TO WIN AT CARDS.

1421
01:05:20,117 --> 01:05:22,387
I LIKE DISPROVING
OLD-FASHIONED SAYINGS.

1422
01:05:22,420 --> 01:05:25,222
THAT ONE ESPECIALLY.

1423
01:05:25,255 --> 01:05:27,492
HOLD THIS.
THANK YOU.

1424
01:05:27,525 --> 01:05:29,327
PLEASE TELL THEM,
MR. CARVER,

1425
01:05:29,360 --> 01:05:31,528
THAT I'M HERE
AS AN HONORED GUEST.

1426
01:05:31,562 --> 01:05:34,598
[SCOFFS] FINE. YOU DON'T
HAVE TO CHIP IN ON THE PIZZA.

1427
01:05:34,632 --> 01:05:35,900
I DON'T QUITE UNDERSTAND.

1428
01:05:35,933 --> 01:05:39,237
BY THE WAY, I HEARD
THE CROUPIER CALL YOU CHARLTON.

1429
01:05:39,270 --> 01:05:41,138
HAVE YOU CHANGED YOUR NAME?

1430
01:05:41,172 --> 01:05:42,940
NO, THERE'S SOME MISTAKE,
I'M AFRAID.

1431
01:05:42,973 --> 01:05:45,208
I'M CHARLTON CHEW.

1432
01:05:45,242 --> 01:05:48,078
MY APOLOGIES, SENORES.

1433
01:05:48,112 --> 01:05:49,880
I'LL JUST TAKE CARE OF THIS,

1434
01:05:49,913 --> 01:05:52,950
AND THEN I'LL RETURN.

1435
01:05:52,983 --> 01:05:54,918
SORRY, DARLING.

1436
01:05:54,952 --> 01:05:56,953
SURE. THAT'S OKAY. FINE.

1437
01:05:56,987 --> 01:05:57,988
COME WITH ME THEN.

1438
01:05:58,022 --> 01:06:01,558
I'LL FIX YOU
A NICE BLACK COW.

1439
01:06:01,592 --> 01:06:03,727
LET'S GO TO
THE FURNITURE SHOWROOM.

1440
01:06:03,760 --> 01:06:05,528
WE'LL GO TO THE BILLIARD ROOM.

1441
01:06:05,562 --> 01:06:09,867
WELL, YOU'RE ALL GONNA BE
BART FARGO-LESS FOR A WHILE.

1442
01:06:09,900 --> 01:06:12,470
I BETTER HAVE
ANOTHER SCREWDRIVER.

1443
01:06:16,207 --> 01:06:19,277
HI, I'M HERE FOR THE WIGLET
SOCIETY MEETING.

1444
01:06:19,310 --> 01:06:22,713
NO?

1445
01:06:22,747 --> 01:06:26,450
THAT FEELS NICE. YEAH.

1446
01:06:26,483 --> 01:06:29,520
YOU THINK YOU KNOW
A GREAT MANY THINGS,
DON'T YOU, FARGO?

1447
01:06:29,553 --> 01:06:31,955
I BROUGHT YOU TO MY PARENTS'
RUMPUS ROOM FOR A REASON.

1448
01:06:31,988 --> 01:06:34,558
BUT KNOWLEDGE CAN BE
EXTREMELY DANGEROUS.

1449
01:06:34,592 --> 01:06:36,560
I KNOW THAT. DUH.

1450
01:06:36,593 --> 01:06:39,130
YOUR GOOD FORTUNE MAY TURN.

1451
01:06:39,163 --> 01:06:41,798
WHY DON'T YOU PUT YOUR CARDS
ON THE TABLE.

1452
01:06:41,832 --> 01:06:43,433
WHAT--YOU'RE PLAYING POOL.

1453
01:06:43,467 --> 01:06:47,438
THIS TIME YOU MIGHT LOSE.

1454
01:06:47,472 --> 01:06:49,373
I'M SORRY TO HAVE
TO DISAPPOINT YOU...

1455
01:06:49,407 --> 01:06:51,408
BUT I'M EILEEN ECKERT.

1456
01:06:51,442 --> 01:06:54,043
BUT I'M NOT IN THE HABIT
OF LOSING.

1457
01:06:54,077 --> 01:06:55,678
YOU WANNA GET
A PICTURE THERE?

1458
01:07:00,250 --> 01:07:02,820
OKAY. HERE WE GO.

1459
01:07:02,853 --> 01:07:04,822
AND...NO, OOH.

1460
01:07:04,855 --> 01:07:07,525
HEY, WE PLAYING CALL?

1461
01:07:07,558 --> 01:07:11,262
I THINK THIS GAME'S
LASTED TOO LONG.

1462
01:07:11,295 --> 01:07:12,295
DON'T YOU, CARVER?

1463
01:07:12,328 --> 01:07:13,763
20 SECONDS?

1464
01:07:13,797 --> 01:07:15,432
THAT'S WHAT I WAS THINKING.

1465
01:07:15,465 --> 01:07:18,768
UH, I THINK.

1466
01:07:18,802 --> 01:07:21,472
HEY, WE HAD OUR QUARTERS
ON THE TABLE.

1467
01:07:24,342 --> 01:07:27,077
GO STEAL THE CHALK.

1468
01:07:27,110 --> 01:07:28,578
IT'S ROLAND GIFT.

1469
01:07:28,612 --> 01:07:30,580
HMM.

1470
01:07:30,613 --> 01:07:34,452
HI.

1471
01:07:34,485 --> 01:07:37,822
IS THAT REALLY...
NICE.

1472
01:07:37,855 --> 01:07:41,758
HA-HA. THE EVER DEBONAIR
BART FARGO.

1473
01:07:41,792 --> 01:07:43,993
EW.
NOW IT SMELLS WEIRD.

1474
01:07:44,027 --> 01:07:47,030
HELLO, DARLING.

1475
01:07:47,063 --> 01:07:49,467
WELL, WELL.

1476
01:07:49,500 --> 01:07:51,702
OLD FRIENDS MEET AGAIN.

1477
01:07:51,735 --> 01:07:55,238
BART. BART?

1478
01:07:55,272 --> 01:07:58,375
BART. BART. BART. BART.

1479
01:07:58,408 --> 01:08:00,945
STOP IT.

1480
01:08:00,978 --> 01:08:02,445
BART, I--

1481
01:08:02,478 --> 01:08:05,917
I--I THINK I'M A HOSTAGE.
HOO, HOO.

1482
01:08:05,950 --> 01:08:08,052
HOW DID YOU FIND OUT
I WAS COMING HERE.

1483
01:08:08,085 --> 01:08:09,920
I HEARD IT ON THE TELEPHONE.

1484
01:08:09,953 --> 01:08:11,855
THE PORTER
GAVE YOU THIS ADDRESS.

1485
01:08:11,888 --> 01:08:15,625
- WHAT PORTER?
- THAT'S NOT IMPORTANT NOW.

1486
01:08:15,658 --> 01:08:18,162
YOU WERE VERY CLEVER,
CARVER.

1487
01:08:18,195 --> 01:08:19,563
KIDNAPPING THE PROFESSOR

1488
01:08:19,597 --> 01:08:21,465
WAS A BRILLIANT
PIECE OF WORK.

1489
01:08:21,498 --> 01:08:23,267
MY CONGRATULATIONS.

1490
01:08:23,300 --> 01:08:27,805
LOOK, LET'S PUT OUR BALLS
ON THE TABLE, SHALL WE?

1491
01:08:27,838 --> 01:08:29,507
THANK YOU, FARGO.

1492
01:08:29,540 --> 01:08:32,475
FOR BEING A MAJOR
AGRICULTURAL CENTER
IN THE UPPER MIDWEST.

1493
01:08:32,508 --> 01:08:34,612
TAKE THEM BOTH TO THE VILLA.

1494
01:08:34,645 --> 01:08:36,547
OH, AND GET
THE PROFESSOR READY.

1495
01:08:36,580 --> 01:08:38,515
AND GILLIGAN AND MARY ANN.

1496
01:08:38,548 --> 01:08:40,650
OH, I WAS HOPING
YOU WOULDN'T SAY THAT.

1497
01:08:40,683 --> 01:08:43,587
SORRY. I'M SORRY.

1498
01:08:55,465 --> 01:08:56,733
HEY, SHOW ME
JUST ONE MORE TIME.

1499
01:08:56,767 --> 01:08:58,468
IT'S VERY SIMPLE.
IT'S JUST LIKE THAT.

1500
01:08:58,502 --> 01:08:59,703
JUST UP...

1501
01:08:59,737 --> 01:09:02,873
MIKE, TOM, THANKS
TO TODAY'S MOVIE,

1502
01:09:02,907 --> 01:09:04,542
I'VE REALIZED
MORE FIRMLY THAN EVER

1503
01:09:04,575 --> 01:09:06,110
THE IMPORTANCE, TO A MAN,

1504
01:09:06,143 --> 01:09:08,445
OF A GOOD PAIR
OF MAN SUNGLASSES.

1505
01:09:08,478 --> 01:09:09,613
LIKE THOSE.

1506
01:09:09,647 --> 01:09:11,348
UH, WHY, YES.

1507
01:09:11,382 --> 01:09:13,617
UH, ONE OF A LINE OF ITALIAN
SUNGLASSES I'VE DEVELOPED.

1508
01:09:13,650 --> 01:09:16,520
UH, CAMBOT,
THE "BAH DAH-DAH DAH-DAH"
MUSIC, PLEASE.

1509
01:09:16,553 --> 01:09:17,688
[JAZZ MUSIC PLAYS]

1510
01:09:17,722 --> 01:09:19,490
THANK YOU.
NOTE HOW THE DELICATE LINES

1511
01:09:19,523 --> 01:09:21,058
SHADE MY SENSITIVE EYES

1512
01:09:21,092 --> 01:09:23,893
FROM THE HARSH AND
WRINKLE-INDUCING MIDDAY SUN.

1513
01:09:23,927 --> 01:09:24,928
I DON'T KNOW.

1514
01:09:24,962 --> 01:09:26,363
THEY SEEM A LITTLE
WOMANY FOR ME.

1515
01:09:26,397 --> 01:09:28,065
- NO, THEY'RE FOR MEN.
- AH.

1516
01:09:28,098 --> 01:09:30,600
MIKE, YOU'LL FIND A LOVELY
BOX UNDER THERE

1517
01:09:30,633 --> 01:09:32,870
FILLED WITH MORE OF MY ITALIAN
SUNGLASSES FOR MEN.

1518
01:09:32,903 --> 01:09:34,338
OOH.

1519
01:09:34,372 --> 01:09:38,208
KEEP IN MIND, THESE WORK BEST IF
YOU'VE GOT A SMALL ITALIAN HEAD.

1520
01:09:38,242 --> 01:09:40,143
OH, THERE'S A LUSCIOUS PAIR.

1521
01:09:40,177 --> 01:09:42,478
NOW THOSE ARE WOMANY.

1522
01:09:42,512 --> 01:09:44,113
EXCEPT THAT THEY'RE FOR MEN.

1523
01:09:44,147 --> 01:09:46,983
YES, THIS MODEL I CALL
THE BRIGITTE BARDOT.

1524
01:09:47,017 --> 01:09:48,685
- SHE'S FRENCH.
- WHATEVER.

1525
01:09:48,718 --> 01:09:50,587
MIKE,
THE POINT IS THESE GLASSES

1526
01:09:50,620 --> 01:09:52,757
ACCENTUATE A MAN'S
OWN SPECIAL FEATURES.

1527
01:09:52,790 --> 01:09:55,458
AND MAYBE HELP US
GET TO A PLACE,

1528
01:09:55,492 --> 01:09:57,895
A SECRET, INNER, MANLY PLACE

1529
01:09:57,928 --> 01:09:59,330
THAT ONLY MEN CAN KNOW.

1530
01:09:59,363 --> 01:10:01,232
AND THEY'RE FOR MEN.

1531
01:10:01,265 --> 01:10:03,167
OF COURSE.
WHO ELSE?

1532
01:10:03,200 --> 01:10:04,835
OH, AND NOW MY FAVORITE,

1533
01:10:04,868 --> 01:10:06,770
THE COLISEUM BY MOONLIGHT.

1534
01:10:06,803 --> 01:10:09,440
OH, YES,
A SHARED GLASS OF ROSé,

1535
01:10:09,473 --> 01:10:11,742
AN INTIMATE EVENING
AND MOVIES ON LIFETIME.

1536
01:10:11,775 --> 01:10:13,610
- NOW THAT'S WOMANY!
- WHAT IS?

1537
01:10:13,643 --> 01:10:15,078
MEN WEAR THESE SUNGLASSES?

1538
01:10:15,112 --> 01:10:18,182
OF COURSE. HOW MANY TIMES
DO I HAVE TO EXPLAIN?

1539
01:10:18,215 --> 01:10:21,252
NOW, IT SEEMS LIKE YOU'D HAVE
TO BE PRETTY CONFIDENT TO...

1540
01:10:21,285 --> 01:10:22,953
I DON'T SEE WHY.

1541
01:10:22,987 --> 01:10:24,655
LOOK, IF YOU GUYS DON'T LIKE

1542
01:10:24,688 --> 01:10:26,790
MY EXCLUSIVE LINE OF SUNGLASSES
FOR ITALIAN MEN,

1543
01:10:26,823 --> 01:10:28,858
THEN THAT'S JUST FINE.

1544
01:10:28,892 --> 01:10:30,760
MAYBE WE'RE NOT
ITALIAN ENOUGH.

1545
01:10:30,793 --> 01:10:32,195
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1546
01:10:32,228 --> 01:10:33,663
PRETTY GOSH DARN WOMANY.

1547
01:10:33,697 --> 01:10:35,765
YEAH, THERE'S SOMETHING
ABOUT 'EM...

1548
01:10:42,205 --> 01:10:45,408
[WHISTLING, HUMMING]

1549
01:10:45,442 --> 01:10:46,610
GET IN.

1550
01:10:46,643 --> 01:10:51,148
AND DON'T SIT
ON MY COMIC BOOKS.

1551
01:10:51,182 --> 01:10:55,918
- OH, NO. POISON PEZ!
- OOH.

1552
01:10:55,952 --> 01:10:59,490
HERBIE, THE MISFIT ELF.

1553
01:10:59,523 --> 01:11:01,425
AAH!

1554
01:11:01,458 --> 01:11:04,428
OH, NO. ONE OF
THE THREE TENORS IS DOWN!

1555
01:11:04,462 --> 01:11:07,698
[LAUGHS]
GOOD.

1556
01:11:07,732 --> 01:11:09,600
HA! IT'S FUN.

1557
01:11:09,633 --> 01:11:11,002
THANKS FOR REPAYING
THAT DEPT.

1558
01:11:11,035 --> 01:11:12,368
CARVER MENTIONED
ANOTHER VILLA.

1559
01:11:12,402 --> 01:11:13,603
DO YOU KNOW WHERE IT IS?

1560
01:11:13,637 --> 01:11:15,138
BUT I CAN'T GO THERE.
I'D BE KILLED.

1561
01:11:15,172 --> 01:11:16,440
I'M DELICATE.

1562
01:11:16,473 --> 01:11:18,008
NO, PLEASE DON'T ASK ME
TO DO THAT.

1563
01:11:18,042 --> 01:11:19,343
SURELY I'VE DONE ENOUGH.
HAVEN'T I?

1564
01:11:19,377 --> 01:11:20,777
HERE'S 3,000 BUCKS.

1565
01:11:20,810 --> 01:11:21,812
STOCK THE VILLA
WITH GROCERIES.

1566
01:11:21,845 --> 01:11:23,047
WHEN WE GET TO THE VILLA,

1567
01:11:23,080 --> 01:11:25,282
I'LL GIVE YOU ANOTHER 3,000.

1568
01:11:25,315 --> 01:11:27,517
AND THEN I PROMISE
TO HELP YOU START A NEW LIFE

1569
01:11:27,550 --> 01:11:29,085
WHEN ALL THIS IS FINISHED.

1570
01:11:29,118 --> 01:11:31,422
COME ON. WE'D BETTER
HIDE THESE CORPSES.

1571
01:11:31,455 --> 01:11:35,958
YOU'D THINK A DECENT HOTEL
WOULD TAKE CARE OF THAT.

1572
01:11:35,992 --> 01:11:37,293
HERE WE GO.

1573
01:11:37,327 --> 01:11:41,298
♪ DRAGGING THE BODIES, YEAH ♪

1574
01:11:41,332 --> 01:11:45,468
♪ HIDING THE EVIDENCE ♪

1575
01:11:45,502 --> 01:11:47,303
♪ HEY,
WE'RE GETTING FUNKY NOW ♪

1576
01:11:47,337 --> 01:11:49,272
YEAH!

1577
01:11:49,305 --> 01:11:51,342
[IMITATING MUSIC]

1578
01:11:51,375 --> 01:11:53,510
MAYBE THE GUARDS AT THE VILLA
KNOW YOU LEFT THE GANG.

1579
01:11:53,543 --> 01:11:55,012
- NO, I DOUBT IT.
- MAYBE WE'RE DWARVES.

1580
01:11:55,045 --> 01:11:56,047
I'M NOT IMPORTANT ENOUGH.

1581
01:11:56,080 --> 01:11:57,447
NO ONE WOULD THINK
OF TELLING THEM.

1582
01:11:57,480 --> 01:12:02,185
[IMITATING MUSIC]

1583
01:12:02,218 --> 01:12:05,422
♪ WATERMELON MAN ♪

1584
01:12:07,423 --> 01:12:11,262
THIS VILLA WILL COMPETE.

1585
01:12:11,295 --> 01:12:15,298
CAN YOU CHECK THIS?
I THINK I'M DONE.

1586
01:12:15,332 --> 01:12:19,603
[IMITATING MUSIC]

1587
01:12:19,637 --> 01:12:21,037
I'M SORRY, MA'AM,

1588
01:12:21,070 --> 01:12:25,042
BUT WE'VE GOTTA GET SOME USE
OUT OF THIS DEATH RAY.

1589
01:12:25,075 --> 01:12:29,413
I'VE GOT AN IMPISH IDEA.
[LAUGHS]

1590
01:12:29,447 --> 01:12:31,415
HI.
I'M STILL IN THE MOVIE.

1591
01:12:31,448 --> 01:12:32,817
THIS DRUG WILL COMPLETELY

1592
01:12:32,850 --> 01:12:34,785
DESTROY YOUR WILLPOWER,
PROFESSOR.

1593
01:12:34,818 --> 01:12:37,220
BY THE TIME
HERR CARVER RETURNS,

1594
01:12:37,253 --> 01:12:38,622
YOU'LL NO LONGER BE ABLE

1595
01:12:38,655 --> 01:12:40,657
TO THINK OR ACT
INDEPENDENTLY.

1596
01:12:40,690 --> 01:12:43,027
YOU'LL BECOME
MICHAEL HUFFINGTON.

1597
01:12:45,295 --> 01:12:47,597
OH. SUDDENLY
THEY'RE IN LAKE ELMO.

1598
01:12:47,630 --> 01:12:49,633
WATCH OUT FOR THIS ROCK.

1599
01:12:59,643 --> 01:13:01,812
I OUGHT TO HIT YOU.

1600
01:13:04,180 --> 01:13:05,915
YOU ARE GOING
TO MILITARY SCHOOL

1601
01:13:05,948 --> 01:13:07,985
WHETHER YOU LIKE IT OR NOT.

1602
01:13:08,018 --> 01:13:09,687
COULD YOU TURN
THE RADIO DOWN?

1603
01:13:09,720 --> 01:13:11,422
I'M REALLY SICK
OF THIS SONG.

1604
01:13:11,455 --> 01:13:13,757
[JAZZ MUSIC]

1605
01:13:13,790 --> 01:13:17,460
AH, THE BEAUTIFUL PEOPLE
LIVE HERE.

1606
01:13:17,493 --> 01:13:18,962
COME ON. HI.

1607
01:13:18,995 --> 01:13:21,132
WELCOME TO JACK RUBY
FANTASY CAMP.

1608
01:13:24,367 --> 01:13:29,005
[SCATTING]

1609
01:13:29,038 --> 01:13:30,373
DON'T WORRY, BART.

1610
01:13:30,407 --> 01:13:33,377
THE NURSES WILL BE
VERY NICE TO YOU HERE.

1611
01:13:33,410 --> 01:13:34,712
WHOA, PARTNER.

1612
01:13:34,745 --> 01:13:38,148
YOU JUST MISSED
THE PINECREST RESORT.

1613
01:13:38,182 --> 01:13:42,318
WELL, WHO'S FOR BADMINTON?

1614
01:13:42,352 --> 01:13:45,388
HE'S STRUMMING
HIS MACHINE GUN.

1615
01:13:45,422 --> 01:13:47,790
HA-HA. HA.

1616
01:13:47,823 --> 01:13:49,292
THE WHOLE DRIVING BY THING

1617
01:13:49,325 --> 01:13:51,528
WENT OFF
EXACTLY AS PLANNED.

1618
01:13:54,397 --> 01:13:56,833
DID YOU MOON HIM?
[LAUGHS]

1619
01:13:56,867 --> 01:13:59,537
I'M NOT SURE WHAT HAPPENED,
BUT I'M DELIGHTED.

1620
01:14:04,140 --> 01:14:06,577
DRIVING MISS FARGO.

1621
01:14:06,610 --> 01:14:09,178
BART?

1622
01:14:10,780 --> 01:14:12,648
OKAY, REMEMBER,
WE'RE JUST LOOKING.

1623
01:14:12,682 --> 01:14:13,883
WE'RE JUST LOOKING
AT THE MODEL.

1624
01:14:13,917 --> 01:14:15,652
WE'RE NOT GONNA BUY.

1625
01:14:17,853 --> 01:14:20,323
GOOD WAY TO SNEAK UP.
SLAM THE DOORS.

1626
01:14:20,357 --> 01:14:21,458
WHAT ARE YOU LOOKING FOR?

1627
01:14:21,492 --> 01:14:22,893
I THOUGHT YOU KNEW.
I DON'T KNOW.

1628
01:14:22,927 --> 01:14:24,928
WHAT--?

1629
01:14:24,962 --> 01:14:27,797
OKAY, NOW REMEMBER
THESE PEOPLE ARE VERY UPTIGHT,

1630
01:14:27,830 --> 01:14:29,600
SO DON'T DO
NONE OF YOUR JEW JOKES.

1631
01:14:29,633 --> 01:14:31,000
IS THAT THE ENTRANCE?

1632
01:14:31,033 --> 01:14:32,835
YEAH, BUT DON'T FORGET
WHAT I TOLD YOU, HUH?

1633
01:14:32,868 --> 01:14:34,270
THAT YOU'RE A TIGER
IN THE SACK?

1634
01:14:34,303 --> 01:14:36,105
SURE WON'T.
DON'T YOU WORRY.

1635
01:14:36,138 --> 01:14:37,908
[JAZZ MUSIC PLAYS]

1636
01:14:37,942 --> 01:14:40,177
UH, YOU MIGHT WANT
TO NOTCH DOWN THE MUSIC

1637
01:14:40,210 --> 01:14:42,512
WHILE I'M TRYING TO SNEAK IN.

1638
01:14:42,545 --> 01:14:45,048
COME ON, PRETTY BOY.

1639
01:14:45,082 --> 01:14:47,450
WATCH BART FARGO ROCK.

1640
01:14:50,287 --> 01:14:51,755
HE HIT BENNY HILL.

1641
01:14:51,788 --> 01:14:53,157
GOOD.

1642
01:14:53,190 --> 01:14:54,992
HEY,
IT'S KIDS IN THE HALL.

1643
01:14:59,963 --> 01:15:00,963
HE WAS NO LADY.

1644
01:15:00,997 --> 01:15:04,802
HE WAS MY WIFE.

1645
01:15:04,835 --> 01:15:06,570
UM, DO WE HAVE A PLAN?

1646
01:15:06,603 --> 01:15:09,238
IT'S TONY CURTIS.

1647
01:15:13,077 --> 01:15:15,112
THE LADIES ARE PUTTY
IN HIS HANDS.

1648
01:15:15,145 --> 01:15:19,215
LET'S SEE. WOULD YOU LOOK GOOD
NEXT TO THE PLANT OR--?

1649
01:15:19,248 --> 01:15:22,618
ALL RIGHT, IN HERE.

1650
01:15:22,652 --> 01:15:24,020
IN THERE.

1651
01:15:24,053 --> 01:15:26,857
NOW I'M GONNA GET
MEDIEVAL ON YOUR ASS.

1652
01:15:28,958 --> 01:15:30,360
YOU'RE IN BED FOR GOOD,
YOUNG MAN.

1653
01:15:30,393 --> 01:15:33,530
NO GETTING UP
FOR A GLASS OF WATER.

1654
01:15:33,563 --> 01:15:37,567
OH, ANOTHER
GREAT HIDING PLACE.

1655
01:15:37,600 --> 01:15:40,737
SUDDENLY THEY'RE ON THE SET
OF THE CHEYENNE SOCIAL CLUB.

1656
01:15:45,208 --> 01:15:48,178
THE DAY THEY KILLED
CHAD AND JEREMY.

1657
01:15:50,180 --> 01:15:52,548
I GOTTA GET
A BIGGER BODY CLOSET.

1658
01:15:57,553 --> 01:15:59,188
NOW, NO TALKING OR GIGGLING,

1659
01:15:59,222 --> 01:16:01,492
OR I'LL SEPARATE
YOU THREE.

1660
01:16:01,525 --> 01:16:03,893
OKAY, I GOTTA
FIGURE SOMETHING OUT HERE.

1661
01:16:03,927 --> 01:16:05,562
I'M CONKING A LOT OF PEOPLE,

1662
01:16:05,595 --> 01:16:07,630
BUT I'M NOT MAKING
ANY HEADWAY.

1663
01:16:14,337 --> 01:16:17,440
OH, NO.
JOEY BISHOP IS DOWN.

1664
01:16:17,473 --> 01:16:20,777
FOUR PEOPLE DOWN,
AND NOT A SINGLE QUIP.

1665
01:16:20,810 --> 01:16:22,745
HE'S GONNA BUMP
INTO MISS KITTY.

1666
01:16:26,182 --> 01:16:29,585
YEAH, I HOPE THEY HAVE A BODY
CLOSET ON THE SECOND FLOOR.

1667
01:16:39,195 --> 01:16:40,263
QUIT FOLLOWING ME.

1668
01:16:40,297 --> 01:16:42,432
GET READY.
CARVER WILL BE HERE SOON.

1669
01:16:42,465 --> 01:16:45,768
RIGHT.

1670
01:16:45,802 --> 01:16:47,803
ONE, TWO,
SKIP TO MY LOU.

1671
01:16:47,837 --> 01:16:48,838
THREE, FOUR...

1672
01:16:48,872 --> 01:16:49,873
OH. THERE THEY GO.

1673
01:16:49,907 --> 01:16:53,143
FIVE, SIX...
[HUMMING]

1674
01:16:53,177 --> 01:16:57,880
OH, YOU'RE HERE! WHOA!

1675
01:16:57,913 --> 01:17:00,383
KEEP IT DOWN OUT HERE,
OR I WILL TELL THE R.A.

1676
01:17:00,417 --> 01:17:02,385
UH, TIME TO SHAVE MY BROW.

1677
01:17:02,418 --> 01:17:03,820
CARL.

1678
01:17:03,853 --> 01:17:06,155
CARL, DO WE HAVE
A CASSEROLE DISH?

1679
01:17:14,230 --> 01:17:15,332
CARL?

1680
01:17:15,365 --> 01:17:17,367
CARL,
WHERE ARE THE CROUTONS?

1681
01:17:20,037 --> 01:17:23,707
MACAULAY CULKIN
IN HOME ALONE 57.

1682
01:17:23,740 --> 01:17:27,943
WELL,
TIME TO RUN INTO A TRAP.

1683
01:17:27,977 --> 01:17:31,848
HAVE YOU SEEN CARL?

1684
01:17:31,882 --> 01:17:33,383
OH, PLEASE.
I'M NOT READY FOR THIS.

1685
01:17:33,417 --> 01:17:35,152
I LIKE YOU
JUST AS A THUG.

1686
01:17:38,322 --> 01:17:40,790
YOU'RE NOT CARL.
CARL DOESN'T HIT ME.

1687
01:17:44,460 --> 01:17:46,897
OH,
AND HE PICKS UP A SPARE.

1688
01:17:49,265 --> 01:17:51,735
SECRET AGENT SPECIALIZES
IN ROUGHHOUSING.

1689
01:17:51,768 --> 01:17:53,103
YOU CAN TELL
THEIR MOM'S GONE.

1690
01:17:53,137 --> 01:17:56,338
UGH! UGH!

1691
01:17:56,372 --> 01:17:57,673
[GRUNTING]

1692
01:17:57,707 --> 01:18:01,010
YOU MUST BE CARL.

1693
01:18:01,043 --> 01:18:04,815
[GROANING]

1694
01:18:09,185 --> 01:18:11,788
YEAH, THAT'S IT.
HIT HIM WITH PICKWICK PAPERS.

1695
01:18:15,325 --> 01:18:17,927
THANKS. NOW I'LL HAVE TO WEAR
A TURTLENECK TO SCHOOL.

1696
01:18:21,665 --> 01:18:26,335
HOW ABOUT A HAND OF POKER?

1697
01:18:26,368 --> 01:18:28,438
OH, NO. THAT ANTIQUE
BREAK-AWAY CHAIR

1698
01:18:28,472 --> 01:18:31,708
HAS BEEN IN THE FAMILY
FOR YEARS.

1699
01:18:31,742 --> 01:18:34,443
YOU KNOW, NEITHER ONE OF US
IS VERY GOOD AT THIS.

1700
01:18:37,380 --> 01:18:39,750
OWWIE. OWWIE.

1701
01:18:46,122 --> 01:18:47,790
[HUMMING]

1702
01:18:47,823 --> 01:18:49,725
THIS WOMAN...

1703
01:18:49,758 --> 01:18:51,862
UGH!

1704
01:18:51,895 --> 01:18:53,397
HE DIED AS HE LIVED--

1705
01:18:53,430 --> 01:18:55,532
NOT REALLY HAVING ANYTHING
TO DO WITH THIS FILM.

1706
01:18:55,565 --> 01:18:57,800
HMM.

1707
01:19:00,137 --> 01:19:01,738
AL.

1708
01:19:01,772 --> 01:19:04,173
HEY, LOOK OUT!

1709
01:19:04,207 --> 01:19:06,977
HEY, YOU SHOT THE GARDNER
AND THE POOL GUY

1710
01:19:07,010 --> 01:19:08,412
AND THE CHEMLAN GUY.

1711
01:19:08,445 --> 01:19:11,748
[MAN GROANS]

1712
01:19:11,782 --> 01:19:16,218
BART,
THOSE WERE OUR PEOPLE.

1713
01:19:16,252 --> 01:19:17,520
I WANT YOU TO KNOW

1714
01:19:17,553 --> 01:19:20,590
HOW MUCH YOUR FOUR LINES
OF DIALOGUE MEANT TO ME.

1715
01:19:20,623 --> 01:19:23,125
THIS HAS THE TONE
OF AN INCREDIBLE HULK EPISODE.

1716
01:19:23,158 --> 01:19:24,760
[JAZZ MUSIC]

1717
01:19:24,793 --> 01:19:26,162
THIS ISN'T
APPROPRIATE RIGHT NOW.

1718
01:19:26,195 --> 01:19:29,332
HIS FRIEND
IS DYING OVER THERE.

1719
01:19:29,365 --> 01:19:30,967
- IT'S NICE.
- IT'S NICE, THOUGH, YEAH.

1720
01:19:31,000 --> 01:19:35,272
[LAUGHS]

1721
01:19:35,305 --> 01:19:37,173
BART FARGO IS...

1722
01:19:37,207 --> 01:19:39,877
HARD TO WATCH.

1723
01:19:39,910 --> 01:19:43,247
HEY, WE'RE JUST
PLAYING CROQUET.

1724
01:19:45,748 --> 01:19:49,818
IF HE HARMS ONE HAIR
ON MY EARRINGS...

1725
01:19:49,852 --> 01:19:51,020
BART FARGO.

1726
01:19:51,053 --> 01:19:53,690
BART FARGO, BART FARGO,
BART FARGO, BART FARGO.

1727
01:19:53,723 --> 01:19:55,458
- THAT'S HARD.
- THAT IS.

1728
01:19:55,492 --> 01:19:59,595
THANK GOD
THIS IS BULLET-PROOF ERMINE.

1729
01:19:59,628 --> 01:20:01,097
HI. YOU DEAD YET?

1730
01:20:01,130 --> 01:20:02,998
AL, HOW DO YOU FEEL?

1731
01:20:03,032 --> 01:20:04,267
ARE YOU URPY?

1732
01:20:04,300 --> 01:20:05,768
I'M SORRY, BART.

1733
01:20:05,802 --> 01:20:08,170
I--THOUGHT--
I THOUGHT I COULD DO IT.

1734
01:20:08,203 --> 01:20:09,405
WHAT? OH, RIGHT.

1735
01:20:09,438 --> 01:20:11,608
YOU'LL BE ALL RIGHT.

1736
01:20:11,642 --> 01:20:14,343
WE'LL JUST GET THAT HALLOWEEN
SCAR ALL CLEANED UP.

1737
01:20:14,377 --> 01:20:16,478
I'M RUNNING OUT ON YOU.

1738
01:20:16,512 --> 01:20:18,748
YOU'LL--YOU'LL HAVE
TO FINISH IT ON YOUR OWN.

1739
01:20:18,782 --> 01:20:21,317
COME ON.
NOW YOU'RE JUST MILKING IT.

1740
01:20:21,350 --> 01:20:22,352
TAKE IT EASY.

1741
01:20:22,385 --> 01:20:26,657
I'M DYING IN A RUSH.

1742
01:20:26,690 --> 01:20:27,690
AAH!

1743
01:20:27,723 --> 01:20:29,425
HEY, WE LOST A TITLEIST--
[GROANS]

1744
01:20:34,130 --> 01:20:36,065
OH. I GUESS THIS THING
WAS PULLING LEFT.

1745
01:20:36,098 --> 01:20:37,600
SORRY! HEH.

1746
01:20:37,633 --> 01:20:41,203
THANKS.
THAT'S SO COMFORTING.

1747
01:20:41,237 --> 01:20:42,805
[JAZZ MUSIC]

1748
01:20:42,838 --> 01:20:44,840
BART FARGO,
BART FARGO, BART FARGO,
BART FARGO, BART FARGO...

1749
01:20:44,873 --> 01:20:48,245
- SHUT UP.
- I JUST LIKE DOING IT.

1750
01:20:52,382 --> 01:20:53,883
WHEN HIS RELATIONSHIPS SOUR,

1751
01:20:53,917 --> 01:20:57,253
HE REALLY LASHES OUT.

1752
01:20:57,287 --> 01:21:01,423
GO ON WITHOUT ME--
OH, YOU DID. OKAY.

1753
01:21:01,457 --> 01:21:02,592
[IMITATING MUSIC]

1754
01:21:02,625 --> 01:21:04,460
BY THE WAY,
IT'S OVER BETWEEN US.

1755
01:21:07,697 --> 01:21:09,967
BART, IT'S OPEN.
JEEZ.

1756
01:21:10,000 --> 01:21:11,133
OH, YEAH, RIGHT.

1757
01:21:11,167 --> 01:21:14,570
STEPHEN HAWKING COULD
HAVE BROKEN THOSE DOORS.

1758
01:21:14,603 --> 01:21:17,273
[SCATTING]

1759
01:21:17,307 --> 01:21:19,943
EVEN THOUGH I'M WATCHING
HIM RIGHT NOW,

1760
01:21:19,977 --> 01:21:21,645
I DON'T REMEMBER HIM.

1761
01:21:21,678 --> 01:21:24,647
BROKE INTO
WES MONTGOMERY'S HOUSE.

1762
01:21:24,680 --> 01:21:27,083
OSCAR PETERSON'S HOUSE.

1763
01:21:27,117 --> 01:21:31,153
BY NOW THE DEATH RAY
IS COMPLETELY FORGOTTEN.

1764
01:21:31,187 --> 01:21:33,188
LIONEL HAMPTON'S HOUSE.

1765
01:21:33,222 --> 01:21:35,358
I HAVE NO IDEA
WHAT I'M DOING,

1766
01:21:35,392 --> 01:21:38,728
BUT I'VE SEEN THIS ALL
IN THE JAMES BOND MOVIES, SO...

1767
01:21:40,197 --> 01:21:41,632
WHOOPS. HEH HEH.

1768
01:21:41,665 --> 01:21:45,335
WRONG FLOOR.

1769
01:21:45,368 --> 01:21:48,838
HEH.
YES. YES, YES, YES, YES.

1770
01:21:48,872 --> 01:21:49,872
YEAH, I LOVE THAT.

1771
01:21:49,905 --> 01:21:51,173
YES.

1772
01:21:51,207 --> 01:21:54,677
I THINK YOU KNOW
WHO JUST DID THAT, DON'T YOU?

1773
01:21:54,710 --> 01:21:59,182
HAVE YOU AND THE DEATH RAY
GOTTEN TO KNOW EACH OTHER?

1774
01:21:59,215 --> 01:22:01,752
JUST WANTED TO FINISH MY
VIDEO GAME BEFORE I KILLED YOU.

1775
01:22:04,387 --> 01:22:07,257
UH, CAN I HAVE
THE LAST BLINTZ?

1776
01:22:09,958 --> 01:22:11,728
LET'S SEE.
YOU ARE HERE.

1777
01:22:11,762 --> 01:22:13,497
WHERE'S BLOOMINGDALE'S?

1778
01:22:17,133 --> 01:22:18,535
I DO ENJOY THIS.

1779
01:22:18,568 --> 01:22:20,737
IT'S A SIMPLE PLEASURE.

1780
01:22:25,975 --> 01:22:27,810
[IMITATING MUSIC]

1781
01:22:27,843 --> 01:22:32,115
YOU'RE WATCHING
THE ALL CHAIR CHANNEL.

1782
01:22:32,148 --> 01:22:34,883
OH, CRAP.
IT'S DANGER!! DEATH RAY.

1783
01:22:34,917 --> 01:22:36,418
I HATE THIS MOVIE.

1784
01:22:36,452 --> 01:22:39,022
COOL, HUH, FOLKS?

1785
01:22:42,325 --> 01:22:43,927
[CHUCKLES]

1786
01:22:43,960 --> 01:22:45,428
YES. YES, YES.

1787
01:22:45,462 --> 01:22:47,397
LITTLE OF THIS HERE.

1788
01:22:47,430 --> 01:22:49,332
YES. YES.

1789
01:22:49,365 --> 01:22:51,033
THERE.

1790
01:22:51,067 --> 01:22:53,202
I GOT INTO
THE COOKING SHERRY.

1791
01:22:53,235 --> 01:22:55,238
[HICCUPS]

1792
01:22:57,873 --> 01:22:59,908
POW.

1793
01:22:59,942 --> 01:23:02,578
OH, THIS IS REALLY
INTERACTIVE TV.

1794
01:23:02,612 --> 01:23:04,380
OH, I DON'T USE THAT
VERY MUCH,

1795
01:23:04,413 --> 01:23:05,548
BUT IT'S WORTH THE MONEY.

1796
01:23:10,253 --> 01:23:12,355
COOL.

1797
01:23:15,392 --> 01:23:18,528
POOPY.

1798
01:23:18,562 --> 01:23:19,962
IS THIS WHAT THEY MEAN

1799
01:23:19,995 --> 01:23:22,565
BY THE DRESSING ROOMS
MAY BE UNDER SURVEILLANCE?

1800
01:23:26,568 --> 01:23:29,305
THE "DOW, DOW, DOW, DOW, DOW"
ATTACHMENT.

1801
01:23:29,338 --> 01:23:31,540
SO THERE'S WHERE
THEY PUT THE CEILING.

1802
01:23:31,573 --> 01:23:34,943
THE CLEVER BASTARDS.

1803
01:23:34,977 --> 01:23:38,548
57 CHANNELS
AND NOTHING'S ALIVE.

1804
01:23:44,320 --> 01:23:47,290
THE DEATH RAY
LOOKS MUTELY ON.

1805
01:23:47,323 --> 01:23:50,693
HE'S SO DREAMY
WHEN HE SHOOTS.

1806
01:23:50,727 --> 01:23:53,497
YOU GOTTA LOVE ME,
DON'T YOU, HUH?

1807
01:23:55,898 --> 01:23:59,535
HMM? HMM? HMM.

1808
01:23:59,568 --> 01:24:03,473
UH, MAYBE I SHOULD HAVE
THOUGHT OF THIS EARLIER.

1809
01:24:05,708 --> 01:24:09,145
MAN, WE ARE TEARING
THROUGH THE CAMERAS.

1810
01:24:09,178 --> 01:24:11,982
DO I HAVE A BIG NOSE?
DO YOU THINK?

1811
01:24:12,015 --> 01:24:15,585
OH, I'M NERVOUS NOW.

1812
01:24:15,618 --> 01:24:19,788
DON'T MOVE
OR THE CURTAIN GETS IT.

1813
01:24:19,822 --> 01:24:22,492
BART FARGO,
BART FARGO, BART FARG--

1814
01:24:22,525 --> 01:24:25,595
THAT IS FUNNY.

1815
01:24:25,628 --> 01:24:27,730
I CAN'T WATCH
ANOTHER EPISODE OF SEAQUEST.

1816
01:24:27,763 --> 01:24:30,367
I MUST DO SOMETHING.

1817
01:24:30,400 --> 01:24:32,302
I CAN SEE
WHY MEN LIKE WOMEN.

1818
01:24:32,335 --> 01:24:34,803
ME TOO.

1819
01:24:34,837 --> 01:24:39,208
TELL MOMMY
WHERE THE GIN IS.

1820
01:24:39,242 --> 01:24:43,547
DANCE WITH ME.

1821
01:24:43,580 --> 01:24:44,847
OH. AAH!

1822
01:24:44,880 --> 01:24:46,515
OKAY, I'LL SLEEP HERE.

1823
01:24:50,953 --> 01:24:53,857
SEE WHAT YOU MADE ME DO?

1824
01:24:53,890 --> 01:24:55,925
THIS MOVIE COULD HAVE
BEEN VERY SUCCESSFUL,

1825
01:24:55,958 --> 01:24:57,427
BUT THEN TALKIES CAME.

1826
01:24:57,460 --> 01:24:59,062
YEAH.

1827
01:24:59,095 --> 01:25:01,597
YOU KNOW,
THEY WERE GONNA CALL THIS
DANGER, WALL-MOUNTED GUNS,

1828
01:25:01,630 --> 01:25:05,368
BUT IT WASN'T
A VERY GOOD TITLE.

1829
01:25:05,402 --> 01:25:07,770
I THINK HAVING A HOUSE
WITH WALL-MOUNTED GUNS

1830
01:25:07,803 --> 01:25:10,105
SHOWS A FEAR OF INTIMACY.

1831
01:25:10,138 --> 01:25:12,808
THIS HOUSE HAS THE GUNS,
BUT NO CENTRAL AIR.

1832
01:25:12,842 --> 01:25:14,110
SO BEWARE.

1833
01:25:14,143 --> 01:25:15,645
HEY,
NICE GRAND FINALE THERE.

1834
01:25:15,678 --> 01:25:17,013
FIREWORKS AND ALL THAT.

1835
01:25:17,047 --> 01:25:19,048
RIGHT NOW I BET THAT GUY'S
GETTING ON THE PHONE

1836
01:25:19,082 --> 01:25:21,517
WITH HIS WALL-GUN
REPRESENTATIVE.

1837
01:25:26,855 --> 01:25:29,858
YEAH, YOU GOTTA SLAP IT IN
LIKE THAT, OR IT DOESN'T WORK.

1838
01:25:29,892 --> 01:25:31,093
YEP. PRETTY MUCH.

1839
01:25:31,127 --> 01:25:33,663
WHATEVER 17TH CENTURY BARON
BUILT THIS PLACE,

1840
01:25:33,697 --> 01:25:35,232
HE HAD SURPRISING
TECHNOLOGY.

1841
01:25:35,265 --> 01:25:38,835
THINK IT WAS JEFFERSON.

1842
01:25:38,868 --> 01:25:40,903
HA.
NOW HE'S AN ART CRITIC.

1843
01:25:43,907 --> 01:25:46,008
OH, I WONDER
IF I TOOK A LEAK RIGHT NOW

1844
01:25:46,042 --> 01:25:47,543
IF I'D BREAK MY MOMENTUM.

1845
